\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr fwds discount narrows on profit taking.   \b0\par\par\uc2 465 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2003\par 06:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Oct 8 (Reuters) - The discount on Hong Kong dollar\par forwards narrowed on Wednesday morning as investors booked\par profits on the back of some dollar bid interest in the spot\par market and a contraction in Chinese yuan non-deliverable forwards\par (NDFs), dealers said.\par     By 0344 GMT, the Hong Kong dollar was trading at 7.7140 per\par U.S. dollar, slightly weaker than the previous session but still\par well above its HK$7.80 pegged exchange rate.\par     "People were looking at spot market trading. The forwards\par discount narrowed when the greenback edged up against the Hong\par Kong dollar."\par     Some traders said the rising USD/HKD spot rate might be due\par to arbitrage trading, as local interest rates are lower than U.S.\par dollar Libor rates.\par     Ample liquidity in the aggregate balance -- which stood at\par HK$3,291 million on Wednesday -- after four \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last\par week by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , has kept interbank\par rates low.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The HKMA has injected a total of HK$2.31 billion to\par try and steady the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par  \par     One-year forwards          were trading at -375/-355 pips,\par narrowed from -410/-395 late on Tuesday.\par     Hong Kong dollar forwards fell to a deeper discount on\par Tuesday in tandem with yuan NDFs on persistent speculation of a\par revaluation of the Chinese yuan.\par     "Market jitters alleviated as Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao said\par China would keep its yuan exchange rate stable," the European\par bank dealer said.\par     One-year yuan NDFs were dealt at -5100/-4,900 points compared\par with -5,300 points late on Tuesday.\par     China manages the yuan in a 8.27-8.28 per dollar range, which\par other countries have criticised as too weak and giving China an\par unfair trade advantage.\par     Dealers said speculation on a move in the yuan has\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 intensified ahead of the APEC leaders summit in Bangkok later   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 this month, in which the region's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  management policies,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 especially those of China, are expected to be raised.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Latest        Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0400 GMT   At 0143 GMT   At 0925 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7130/40     7.7128/31     7.7097/100\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -165 / -155   -170 / -160   -185 / -165\par     Six-month        -270 / -260   -290 / -270   -320 / -300\par     One-year         -375 / -355   -390 / -370   -410 / -395\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight        0.05 / 0.06   0.03 / 0.09   0.12 / 0.18\par     Three-month      0.18 / 0.21   0.18 / 0.25   0.18 / 0.25\par     Six-month        0.31 / 0.33   0.37 / 0.43   0.37 / 0.43\par     One-year         0.73 / 0.75   0.75 / 0.82   0.72 / 0.75\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par Reuters contributor page .\par     (US$=HK$7.8).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031008dza8000rw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
