\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr remains strong on Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  strength.   \b0\par\par\uc2 605 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2003\par 04:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Oct 8 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar remained\par well above its pegged exchange rate to the U.S. dollar on\par Wednesday although slightly down on the previous session, buoyed\par by strength in several Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Hong Kong dollar stood at HK$7.7124/34 per U.S. dollar at\par 9.06 a.m. (0106 GMT) compared with its HK$7.80 pegged exchange\par rate. The local unit was trading at HK$7.7105 on Tuesday\par afternoon in Hong Kong.\par     Dealers said the local unit strengthened to HK$7.7065\par overnight, slightly weaker than the HK$7.7020 level reached last\par Friday, the Hong Kong dollar's strongest level since the 1997/98\par Asian financial crisis.\par     The local unit had strengthened to around HK$7.50 in October\par 1997 as investors poured into Hong Kong dollars while regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tanked against the greenback.\par     "There's still more potential for a strengthening of the Hong\par Kong dollar as Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remain strong," said a dealer at\par a local bank.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "We're still seeing hot money flowing in as Chinese people in\par Indonesia and Thailand see some concrete reasons to come here,"\par the dealer said.\par     The Hong Kong government has said it will give residency\par status to investors who bring in HK$6.5 million and keep the\par money here for seven years.\par     The discount on Hong Kong dollar one-year forwards stood at\par -395/-375 in early trade, from -410/-395 late on Tuesday,\par pointing to market expectations of a further strengthening in the\par spot Hong Kong dollar rate.\par     The Singapore dollar rose to four-month peaks and the Thai\par baht set three-year highs on Wednesday morning, tracking the U.S.\par dollar's overnight fall to fresh lows against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "Whilst the move in the Hong Kong dollar is not driven by\par local fundamentals, economic growth signals are becoming more\par positive with domestic demand rebounding and deflation easing,"\par research group 4cast said in a report.\par  \par     Hong Kong has suffered from about five years of deflation and\par continues to experience near record unemployment.\par     The Hong Kong dollar strengthened sharply against the U.S.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar late last month along with many other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 following the Group of Seven nations' call for more flexible   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 exchange rates.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But recent moves by Beijing to help prop up the Hong Kong   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economy following massive civil protests in July have provided a   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strong incentive for investors to buy Hong Kong dollars.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This has squeezing out other investors who had taken bets   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would depreciate over the next year or so given   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the government's large budget deficit.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains well above its pegged exchange   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rate despite several \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary   \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recently to try to bring the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  back to its fixed   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 level. The government has repeatedly said it remains committed to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 maintaining the 20-year-old peg, seen as the bedrock of the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 territory's financial stability.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0143 GMT   At 0925 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7128/31     7.7097/100\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -170 / -160   -185 / -165\par     Six-month        -290 / -270   -320 / -300\par     One-year         -390 / -370   -410 / -395\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight        0.03 / 0.09   0.12 / 0.18\par     Three-month      0.18 / 0.25   0.18 / 0.25\par     Six-month        0.37 / 0.43   0.37 / 0.43\par     One-year         0.75 / 0.82   0.72 / 0.75\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par Reuters contributor page .\par     (US$=HK$7.8).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031008dza80006q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
