\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr fwds discount deepens on flush liquidity.   \b0\par\par\uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2003\par 12:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Oct 7 (Reuters) - The discount on Hong Kong dollar\par forwards deepened further on Tuesday amid excess liquidity and\par persistent speculation of a revaluation of the Chinese yuan,\par dealers said.\par     "Forwards fell sharply in the afternoon in tandem with a\par deepening discount in Chinese yuan non-deliverable forwards\par (NDFs)," said a dealer from a Japanese bank.\par     "There was talk in the market that Beijing would widen its\par trading band within one to two months, leading the short-dated\par NDFs discount to widen. But I don't believe the news as China has\par repeatedly said it will keep the yuan stable," the dealer said.\par     Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao told business leaders in Bali on\par Tuesday that China would keep its yuan exchange rate basically\par stable but would seek an appropriate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regime.\par     China has come under criticism from the United States and\par other countries for the yuan's current level, which they regard\par as too cheap -- pegged at around 8.28 to the U.S.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar --\par giving Chinese exporters an unfair advantage.\par     Dealers said speculation on a move in the yuan has\par intensified ahead of the APEC leaders summit in Bangkok later\par this month, in which the region's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  management policies,\par especially those of China, are expected to be raised.\par  \par     One-year Chinese yuan NDFs           were dealt at a premium\par of -5,300 points per U.S. dollar level late on Tuesday.\par     Growing international pressure on Beijing to revalue its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has also fuelled expectations that Hong Kong will move\par with China as the two economies become more closely integrated.\par     One-year Hong Kong dollar forwards          settled at\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -410/-395 at 0925 GMT, the lowest level since August 2000, versus   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -370/-350 pips at the end of the morning session and -320/-300   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 pips late on Monday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hong Kong dollar remains strong but some dealers   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said upwards momentum would be limited with some investors   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 unwilling to hold the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  due to falling interbank and   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 deposit rates of interest.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By 1010 GMT, the Hong Kong dollar was trading at 7.7105   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the U.S. unit, compared with 7.7140 at 0905 GMT on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monday, and well above its linked exchange rate of 7.80 to the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 greenback.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Increased liquidity in the aggregate balance - which stood   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 at HK$3,294 million on Tuesday - after four \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 week by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , has kept interbank   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rates low. The HKMA has injected a total of HK$2.31 billion to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 try and steady the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Short-dated interbank rates traded close to zero percent,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dealers said. "If interest rates stay at such low levels for a   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 certain period of time, I'm sure people will start to buy back   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the U.S. dollar and sell the Hong Kong dollar," another dealer   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The local dollar has strengthened over the past weeks as   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 growing signs of economic recovery attract fund inflows into the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 territory's stock market.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0925 GMT   At 0240 GMT   At 0818 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7097/100    7.7088/93     7.7172/75\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -185 / -165   -175 / -165   -175 / -165\par     Six-month        -320 / -300   -280 / -270   -280 / -260\par     One-year         -410 / -395   -350 / -320   -320 / -300\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight        0.12 / 0.18   0.03 / 0.06   0.06 / 0.09\par     Three-month      0.18 / 0.25   0.18 / 0.25   0.18 / 0.25\par     Six-month        0.37 / 0.43   0.37 / 0.43   0.40 / 0.46\par     One-year         0.72 / 0.75   0.75 / 0.87   0.85 / 0.90\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par Reuters contributor page .\par     (US$=HK$7.8).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031007dza7001kw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
