\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr rangebound, forwards discount widens.   \b0\par\par\uc2 441 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2003\par 06:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Oct 7 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar remained\par strong on Tuesday morning but dealers said upwards momentum would\par be limited with some investors unwilling to hold the local\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  due to falling interbank and deposit rates of interest.\par     "I noticed some limited U.S. dollar buying in early trade as\par short-term interest rates fell near to zero percent," said a\par dealer from a European bank.\par  \par     However, he added there was some selling as soon as the Hong\par Kong dollar stepped above 7.7140.\par     By 0255 GMT, the Hong Kong dollar was trading at 7.7100\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the U.S. unit, compared with 7.7140 at 0905 GMT on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Monday, and well above its linked exchange rate of 7.80 to the   \par \par \uc2 greenback.   \par \par \uc2 Increased liquidity in the aggregate balance - which stood   \par \par \uc2 at HK$3,294 million on Tuesday - after four \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last   \par \par \uc2 week by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has kept interbank   \par \par \uc2 rates low. The HKMA has injected a total of HK$2.31 billion to   \par \par \uc2 try and steady the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The overnight to short-week rates were trading below 0.1\par percent, dealers said.\par     "If interest rates stay at such low levels for a certain\par period of time, I'm sure people will start to buy back the U.S.\par dollar and sell the Hong Kong dollar," another dealer said.\par     The local dollar has strengthened over the past weeks as\par growing signs of economic recovery attract fund inflows into the\par territory's stock market.\par     The upwards move was also hastened by a strong rise for Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the wake of last month's G7 meeting urging exchange\par rate flexibility.\par     The discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards widened and dealers\par expected the one-year contracts to head towards -400 pips.\par     "Further downside is expected amid ample liquidity and on\par hopes of a continued inflow of funds," one trader said.\par     One-year forwards          were trading around -370/-350 at\par 0330 GMT, versus -320/-300 pips late on Monday.\par                      Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0240 GMT   At 0818 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7088/93     7.7172/75\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -175 / -165   -175 / -165\par     Six-month        -280 / -270   -280 / -260\par     One-year         -350 / -320   -320 / -300\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight        0.03 / 0.06   0.06 / 0.09\par     Three-month      0.18 / 0.25   0.18 / 0.25\par     Six-month        0.37 / 0.43   0.40 / 0.46\par     One-year         0.75 / 0.87   0.85 / 0.90\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par Reuters contributor page .\par     (US$=HK$7.8).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031007dza7000ma\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
