\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr weakens slightly, seen capped at 7.72 for now.   \b0\par\par\uc2 684 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2003\par 12:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Oct 6 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar weakened\par slightly on Monday as the U.S. dollar gained ground, but remained\par well above its pegged exchange rate to the greenback as foreign\par funds continued to pour into the surging stock market.\par     Dealers remained wary about the direction of the U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and skittish after four \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The HKMA injected a total of HK$2.31 billion to try to\par stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "Some people booked profits after a rebound in dollar/yen,"\par one trader said. The U.S. dollar firmed after last week's\par surprisingly strong U.S. jobs data spurred hopes for a stronger\par economic recovery.\par     The Hong Kong dollar shuffled between 7.71-7.72 for much of\par the day. At 0905 GMT it was trading at 7.7140 against the U.S.\par dollar, versus 7.7020 in the New York session on Friday and\par compared with its linked exchange rate of 7.80.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The local dollar has strengthened over the past weeks as\par growing signs of economic recovery attract fund inflows into the\par territory's stock market, which surged to a fresh 16-month high\par on Monday.\par     Some traders who had speculated that the local dollar would\par weaken in the medium to longer term were caught short by the\par unusually sharp appreciation and were forced to buy back dollars\par at much stronger levels, magnifying the move.\par     Dealers said there was persistent speculation that some\par players were still short the Hong Kong dollar. The longer the\par Hong Kong dollar remains stronger than its pegged level, the\par greater their potential exposure to global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility.\par  \par     One dealer from a European bank said he expected the Hong\par Kong dollar to move between 7.70-7.73 in the near term.\par     Pressure has also been growing on several Asian countries to\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 allow their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to appreciate since the Group of Seven   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 industrial nations urged exchange rate flexibility last month.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers said this month's APEC summit in Bangkok is expected to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 generate more debate on China's yuan policy.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong dollar forwards were rangebound. One-year contracts   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 were trading around -320/-300 pips by late afternoon,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 versus -300/-280 pips at the end of the morning. That compared to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a low at -350 pips in New York trade on Friday - the lowest   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 level since August 2000 - and -240/-220 pips at the end of the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian day on Friday.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The European bank dealer said the market players were\par position to sell the longer-dated forwards.\par     "One- to three-month forwards were very soft as the\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 short-term rates low amid ample liquidity in the market. To run   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the yield curve, the only method is to sell the nine-month and   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 one-year forwards," the dealer said.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     He said one-year contracts may trade as low as -400 pips in\par near term.\par     Increased liquidity in the aggregate balance pushed interbank\par rates lower, dealers said.\par     The HKMA forecasts the aggregate balance -- a key measure of\par interbank liquidity -- to rise to HK$3.29 billion at settlement\par on Tuesday.\par     The overnight interbank rate was quoted at 0.06-0.09 percent\par late on Monday.\par                      Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0818 GMT   At 0330 GMT   At 0945 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7172/75     7.7190/7.72   7.7150/52\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month     -175 / -165    -175 / -165   -160 / -145\par     Six-month       -280 / -260    -270 / -250   -220 / -210\par     One-year        -320 / -300    -300 / -280   -240 / -220\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight       0.06 / 0.09    0.16 / 0.12   0.12 / 0.18\par     Three-month     0.18 / 0.25    0.18 / 0.25   0.30 / 0.37\par     Six-month       0.40 / 0.46    0.40 / 0.43   0.55 / 0.62\par     One-year        0.85 / 0.90    0.85 / 0.88   0.87 / 0.93\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par Reuters contributor page .\par     (US$=HK$7.8).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031006dza6001fm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
