\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-HK dlr weakens slightly as U.S. dollar firms.   \b0\par\par\uc2 605 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2003\par 07:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     HONG KONG, Oct 6 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar weakened\par slightly on Monday morning but remained well above its pegged\par exchange rate to the U.S. dollar as it rode its strongest levels\par since the 1997/98 Asian financial crisis.\par     By 0340 GMT, the Hong Kong dollar was trading at 7.7191\par against the U.S. dollar versus 7.7020 in the New York session on\par Friday, compared with its linked exchange rate of 7.80. The U.S.\par dollar firmed after last week's surprisingly strong U.S. jobs\par data.\par     "In the Asian market, the spot rate usually trades a little\par higher because of some corporate demand for U.S. dollars," said a\par dealer from a Japanese bank.\par     "But I think some people will still maintain short positions\par (on U.S. dollars) at high levels. This is mainly because there is\par appreciation pressure on Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and APEC will meet at\par the end of the month when U.S. President George W. Bush may\par pressure China to revalue the yuan," the dealer added.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     He expected the Hong Kong dollar to trade between\par 7.7000-7.7350 in the near term.\par     The Hong Kong dollar has strengthened over the past weeks as\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 growing signs of economic recovery attract fund inflows into the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 territory's stock market, which recently surged to a 16-month   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 high.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some traders who had speculated that the local dollar would   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 weaken in the medium to longer term were caught short by the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 unusually sharp appreciation and were forced to buy back dollars   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 at much stronger levels, intensifying the move.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pressure has also been growing on several Asian countries to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 allow their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to appreciate since the Group of Seven   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 industrial nations urged exchange rate flexibility last month.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers said this month's APEC summit in Bangkok is expected to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 generate more debate on China's yuan policy.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Slight weakness in the Hong Kong dollar spot rate spurred\par profit taking in the Hong Kong dollar forwards market.\par     One-year contracts          were quoted at -300/-280 pips,\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 versus -350 pips in New York trade on Friday - the lowest level   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 since August 2000 - and -240/-220 pips at the end of the Asian   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 day on Friday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some dealers said discounts were tracking moves in Chinese   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 yuan non-deliverable forwards (NDFs). One-year yuan NDFs were   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dealt at -4,350 points, compared to -4,500 points late on Friday.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Increased liquidity in the aggregate balance pushed interbank\par rates lower, dealers said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the territory's de facto\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  four times last week, injecting a total\par of HK$2.31 billion to try to stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The HKMA forecasts the aggregate balance -- a key measure of\par interbank liquidity -- to rise to HK$3.29 billion at settlement\par on Tuesday.\par     The overnight rate was quoted at 0.06-0.12 percent and a\par major player was reported releasing liquidity early in the\par session.\par                      Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0330 GMT   At 0945 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7190/7.72   7.7150/52\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -175 / -165   -160 / -145\par     Six-month        -270 / -250   -220 / -210\par     One-year         -300 / -280   -240 / -220\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight        0.16 / 0.12   0.12 / 0.18\par     Three-month      0.18 / 0.25   0.30 / 0.37\par     Six-month        0.40 / 0.43   0.55 / 0.62\par     One-year         0.85 / 0.88   0.87 / 0.93\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par Reuters contributor page .\par     (US$=HK$7.8).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031006dza6000j6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
