\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr slightly weaker, remains above peg.   \b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2003\par 03:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Oct 6 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar, experiencing its strongest levels since the 1997/98 Asian financial crisis, weakened slightly early on Monday morning but remained well above its pegged exchange rate to the U.S. dollar.    \par \par \uc2  "The trend for the Hong Kong dollar is going to remain strong," said a dealer at a medium-sized local bank.    \par \par \uc2  "The G7 statement last month, the strength in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Hong Kong government's policies of encouraging more immigrants to invest here, are all creating a lot of demand for Hong Kong dollars," he said.    \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar was trading at HK$7.7120/25 per U.S. dollar at 9.41 a.m. (0141 GMT), weaker than its late Friday level of HK$7.7059, but still far stronger than the HK$7.80 fixed exchange rate set by the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to a high of HK$7.7030 in overnight trade, its strongest since October 1997.    \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar rose against the Japanese yen and the euro after Friday's surprisingly strong U.S. jobs data.    \par \par \uc2  The HKMA, the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  four times last week, injecting a total of more than HK$2.3 billion (US$295 million) to try to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2  Despite maintaining that the Hong Kong government remains committed to maintaining the 20-year-old peg, the HKMA has failed to bring the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to its pegged level.    \par \par \uc2  "We are still seeing inflows of hot money, and as Hong Kong is the most liquid market in east Asia apart from Japan, I would expect the Hong Kong dollar to remain strong for the next couple of weeks," said a dealer at a European bank.    \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar has been reeling ever since the Group of Seven major industrialised economies called for flexible exchange rates on September 20, a move interpreted as a call for Asian nations to stop propping up the dollar for the sake of their exports.    \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong unveiled a money-for-residency programme on September 30 to woo rich foreign investors, saying it would bring in badly-needed cash to help reinvigorate the territory's struggling domestic economy.    \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong dollar forwards remained at a deep discount despite last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reflecting market expectations of further strengthening in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar rate.    \par \par \uc2  The one-year forwards contract stood at -310/-290, slightly higher than the -360/-320 level reached late on Friday, their lowest level since August 2000.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031006dza6000eg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
