\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  again but HK dollar remains strong.   \b0\par\par\uc2 449 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2003\par 14:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oct 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a fourth time in two days late on Friday to try to stabilise the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it remained stubbornly strong against the U.S. dollar, to which it is pegged.   \par \par \uc2 "We have made another injection. We bought US$100 million," a Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokeswoman told Reuters, adding that it had sold \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars in the process.   \par \par \uc2 But after the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar spot rate stood at HK$7.7059/80 at 1210 GMT, only marginally weaker than HK$7.7050 reached last week. That was its strongest level since the Asian financial crisis of 1997-98, and far stronger than its pegged exchange rate of HK$7.80 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Growing international pressure on Beijing to revalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also fuelled expectations that Hong Kong will move with China as the two economies become more closely integrated.   \par \par \uc2 In the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the HKMA sold HK$771 million (US$98.85 million) in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It sold a total of HK$1.54 billion (US$197 million) on Friday in addition to HK$773 on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Despite the rise in the Hong Kong dollar, the HKMA said it remained committed to maintaining the 20-year-old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg.   \par \par \uc2 "(The peg) is the linchpin of Hong Kong's monetary and financial stability and an important factor in Hong Kong's economic success," the spokeswoman told Reuters by phone from a prepared statement.   \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar rose on Friday along with other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a weakened U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the non-deliverable market priced in a rise of over five percent in the Chinese yuan in the next year.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the rise in the yuan's one-year NDF premium was fuelled by speculation that China's policy of managing the yuan in a 8.2760/8.2800 per dollar range would be raised at this month's meeting of APEC leaders.   \par \par \uc2 Chinese yuan one-year non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) rose to a record premium of 4,200 points to the U.S. dollar on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar has remained strong over the past week after soaring to 7.7050 per U.S. dollar in New York. It moved up after a statement from the G7 industrial nations meeting urging exchange rate flexibility.   \par \par \uc2 Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped to bring \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar forwards and interbank rates down.   \par \par \uc2 One-year Hong Kong dollar forwards were trading around -360/-320 pips, their lowest level since August 2000, compared with -135/-125 pips late on Thursday.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031003dza3001rz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
