\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr stronger despite further HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 536 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2003\par 12:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Oct 3 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again on Friday afternoon to try and steady the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong\par Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar, adding another HK$772 million (US$98.9 million) of\par liquidity after the HK unit rose with other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     By 0940 GMT, the Hong Kong dollar was trading at 7.7145\par against the U.S. dollar versus 7.7335 in the morning,\par strengthening despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and well above its linked\par exchange rate of 7.80.\par     This is the third time in two days that the HKMA, the\par territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , has tried to bring the Hong\par Kong dollar back towards its peg with the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The HKMA raised its forecast for the aggregate balance -- a\par key measure of interbank liquidity -- to HK$2,523 million at\par settlement on Tuesday, from HK$1,751 million on Monday.\par     The Hong Kong dollar rose on Friday along with other Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against a weakened U.S.\par    \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as the\par non-deliverable market priced in a rise of over five percent in\par the Chinese yuan in the next year.\par  Dealers said the rise in the yuan's one-year NDF premium was\par fuelled by speculation that China's policy of managing the yuan\par in a 8.2760/8.2800 per dollar range would be raised at this\par month's meeting of APEC leaders.\par  \par     Chinese yuan one-year non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) rose to\par a record premium of 4,200 points to the U.S. dollar on Friday.\par     "The Hong Kong dollar strengthened further following the rise\par in regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said a dealer at a European bank.\par     "If dollar/yen breaks 110, there will be more upwards\par pressure on Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     The Hong Kong dollar has remained strong over the past week\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 after soaring to 7.7050 per U.S. dollar in New York trade last   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monday. It moved up after a statement from the G7 industrial   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 nations meeting urging exchange rate flexibility.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Friday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  helped bring \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar forwards\par and interbank rates down.\par     One-year Hong Kong dollar forwards          were trading\par around -240/-220 pips, their lowest level since November 2000,\par compared with -135/-125 pips late on Thursday.\par     Growing international pressure on Beijing to revalue its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has also fuelled expectations that Hong Kong will move\par with China as the two economies become more closely integrated.\par                      Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0945 GMT   At 0330 GMT   At 0800 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7150/52     7.7320/25       7.7373/80\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -160 / -145   -120 / -110   -100 / - 95\par     Six-month        -220 / -210   -160 / 