\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  again to steady HK dollar.   \b0\par\par\uc2 426 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2003\par 06:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Oct 3 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  yet again in an attempt to steady the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par dollar, adding another HK$386 million (US$49.48 million) of\par liquidity in overnight trade.\par  \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  helped bring HK interbank rates and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong\par Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar forwards down on Friday morning.\par     However, a dealer at a European bank said that despite the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar strengthened to 7.72 after\par breaking 7.73, reflecting a continued inflow of funds."\par     By 0330 GMT, the Hong Kong dollar was trading back at 7.7325\par per U.S. dollar, still well above its linked exchange rate of\par 7.80.\par     The HKMA has revised its forecast for the aggregate balance\par -- a key measure of interbank liquidity -- to HK$1,751 million at\par settlement on Monday, from HK$978 million on Friday.\par     The Hong Kong dollar has remained strong over the past week\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 after soaring to 7.7050 per U.S. dollar in New York trade last   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Monday. It moved up after a statement from the G7 industrial   \par \par \uc2 nations meeting urging exchange rate flexibility.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The overnight to one-year interbank rates were trading below\par one percent, while the forwards rates fell to a deeper discount.\par     One-year forwards          were trading around -170/-160 pips\par after hitting -190 pips in early trade -- a 2-=   year low --\par versus -135/-125 pips late on Thursday.\par     Some dealers said the HK dollar was being bolstered by a\par continued inflow of funds amid persistent U.S. dollar weakness\par and on speculation of a revaluation of the Chinese yuan.\par     Growing international pressure on Beijing to revalue its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has also fuelled expectations that Hong Kong will move\par with China as the two economies become more closely integrated.\par     Chinese yuan one-year non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) rose to\par a record premium of 4,000 points to the U.S. dollar on Friday.\par                      Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0330 GMT   At 0800 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7320/25       7.7373/80\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -120 / -110   -100 / - 95\par     Six-month        -160 / -150   -137 / -127\par     One-year         -170 / -160   -140 / -125\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight        0.12 / 0.25   0.18 / 0.25\par     Three-month      0.37 / 0.50   0.58 / 0.63\par     Six-month        0.50 / 0.62   0.73 / 0.78\par     One-year         0.81 / 0.93   0.97 / 1.03\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par Reuters contributor page .\par     (US$=HK$7.8).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031003dza3000jo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
