\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  In HK Dlr Mkt, Sells HK$772 Mln  \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2003\par 10:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar market for the fourth time in two weeks to stem upward pressure on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold HK$772 million late afternoon when the U.S. dollar fell to around HK$7.7197. The spot rate rebounded slightly after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and was quoted at around HK$7.7195 at 0850 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA's latest move comes after it sold HK$773 million Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the impact of the HKMA's action to be limited. Capital inflows and short-covering of the Hong Kong dollar will dominate the market near term, keeping downward pressure on the spot rate, they said.  \par \par \uc2 Speculation China will in future allow the yuan to appreciate against the U.S. dollar led to the upward pressure on the Hong Kong dollar, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 China and Hong Kong's economies are closely tied and both their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are linked to the U.S. dollar at a fixed rate.  \par \par \uc2 The discount on \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar forwards widened further following the HKMA's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The increase in excess funds in the market put further downward pressure on Hong Kong interbank offered rates, widening the gap between Hibors and U.S. dollar London interbank offered rates.  \par \par \uc2 A bigger differential between Hong Kong and U.S. interest rates leads to a widening of the discounts on forwards.  \par \par \uc2 The one-year forward was quoted at a discount of around 240 to 230 basis points to the spot rate late Friday, compared with a discount of 140 to 130 late Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Raymond Tsoi, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; raymond.tsoi@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Andrew Bullard  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031003dza3000au\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
