\par\par \b \uc2  CHINA WATCH: Yuan Policy May Make Inflation Fresh Risk \b0\par\par\uc2  By James T. Areddy \par \uc2 1,017 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 2003\par 06:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  A Dow Jones Newswires Column \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- China, so often accused of foisting deflation on the rest of world, itself now faces inflation risks. \par \par \uc2  A number of signs suggest price rises are quickly taking hold, prompting a debate framed around China's exchange rate policy. At issue is whether China is trending toward a normal, controllable pickup in prices or the kind of runaway inflation the country endured in the late 1980s and early 1990s. How intense it gets could ultimately determine whether Beijing adjusts the yuan's exchange rate upward. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Federal Reserve Board Chairman Alan Greenspan suggested this month China's exchange rate policy might make the economy overheat. Domestic debt traders see a similar risk, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will need to crack down hard on credit and money supply growth to keep inflation at bay. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  even re-engineered its monetary policy mechanism in April to better deflect inflation with a bill-issuance program that improves its footing to handle the dollar onslaught. It is also waging a verbal campaign to cool property prices and bank lending. \par \par \uc2  Figures bear out signs that price pressure is building. Money supply and lending have each surged over 20% in recent months, and the local bond market is discomforted that severe acute respiratory syndrome tripped the economy less than expected. \par \par \uc2  China's consumer price index recorded inflation each month in the first half of 2003, rising in June to 0.6% above the year-earlier level. The rebound follows years of anemic pricing, the result of ferocious competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  Outright deflation gripped the economy in 2002. Declines in the CPI for 11 of 12 months last year sparked global worries deflation was China's newest and most dangerous export. The International Monetary Fund's website has 143 documents linking "China" and "deflation." \par \par \uc2  Foreign economists tend to be skeptical of the worry about overheating, partly because the flip in sentiment has been so abrupt. Also, prices are still falling on some important products, like mobile phones and other manufactured consumer goods. \par \par \uc2  "We don't see enough evidence to substantiate the argument," according to a recent report by Yiping Huang, a Citigroup Inc. economist in Hong Kong. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Is Departure Point\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy is a major departure point for views on the\par extent of inflation risk - an increasingly politicized and global debate\par over how much the yuan's current under-valuation matters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Many of those optimistic the money supply expansion will be easily\par contained are betting Beijing will adjust rules that govern its exchange\par rate regime, if not allow the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rise outright.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Others are saying China will increasingly challenge a textbook\par economic theory that policy makers can control only one of either the\par exchange rate or interest rates, not both.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Almost every dollar that enters China is exchanged into about 8.3\par yuan. These new yuan are a potential ingredient in inflation, and\par whether they get into the economy is critical to the issue of\par overheating.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The way China is choosing to handle the new yuan currently bucks\par conventional economics. To keep the yuan exchange rate unchanged, the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issues short-term debt instruments to buy back the new yuan\par from banks, which keeps banks from pumping it into the economy and\par kindling inflation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the People's Bank of China doesn't give the market much power to\par determine the interest rate on those bills, maintaining for itself\par control over the exchange and interest rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The situation wasn't much of a problem until prices started to rise,\par since deflation made any rate of interest worthwhile. But now, prices\par are picking up - in conjunction with a huge upsurge in foreign trade and\par investment during the past year that has sent U.S. dollars hurling into\par China at unprecedented speed.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These factors together suggest the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should lift the rates\par it pays on the bills used to mop up the yuan or let the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rise.\par But it isn't complying.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fed Chairman Greenspan hinted that the unconventional lock-hold on\par both interest and exchange rates is China's root problem during recent\par congressional testimony, when he said the situation is something\par "they'll have to address."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Rule Changes\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's extraordinary US$15 billion stock market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par 1998 was a direct outgrowth of a failed attempt to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par fixed and interest rates low in defiance of the theory.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Speculators backed the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  into a corner with\par an elaborate bet it couldn't sustain the policy, and the authority\par escaped only by using shock treatment on traders expecting a more\par conventional reaction to their meddling, such as a devaluation.\par Afterward, a bruised HKMA quickly abandoned trying to determine interest\par rates, so it could focus solely on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign economists don't doubt the conundrum on interest and exchange\par rates exists for China too. But they argue China makes hash of the\par theory since use of the yuan is governed by rules. It isn't fully\par convertible like the Hong Kong dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In effect, China has a third lever: rule changes.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If Beijing were to permit normalized exchange in the yuan, more exit\par strategies for foreign investors, foreign investment for Chinese\par companies in a qualified domestic institutional investor program or a\par more wide-open import regime, some inflationary pressure could be offset\par by the reduction in net U.S. dollar intake. A number of such steps\par already have been taken, and more were outlined Friday in Hong Kong with\par plans to allow more Chinese to travel overseas, and buy foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par for their travels.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Technical changes in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  settlement mechanism and\par QDII are both conceivable," although not necessarily needed now, said Ma\par Qiang, head of research at the Shanghai branch of the PBOC.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -James T. Areddy, Dow Jones Newswires; (86) 1370-1700-594;\par james.areddy@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (With Linda Lin, Dow Jones Newswires; djnews.shanghai@dowjones.com)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Edited by George B. Thomas\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1186 4252 70701 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030728dz7s00089\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
