\par\par \b \uc2  Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Dn Late; Dlr Overcomes Bearish News \b0\par\par\uc2  By Alan Yonan Jr. \par \uc2 799 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2002\par 10:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The dollar held firm against most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday despite a new round of seemingly dollar-bearish news out of the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Only the South Korean won and Thai baht resisted the dollar's advance to finish stronger. \par \par \uc2  Another down day on Wall Street Friday combined with the government's report of a wider-than-expected May trade gap set the stage for a potential dollar pullback when Asian markets opened Monday. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar held its ground in the region, led by solid gains against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's resilience in the face of the negative news suggests that market players may have simply overextended their short-dollar positions during the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent slump, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Until there are signs that the stock market is stabilizing and the U.S. is getting its current account deficit and corporate accounting problems under control, the dollar will have a difficult time making any sustained headway, they added. \par \par \uc2  The won was the big mover during Asian hours, powering its way to a 20-month high against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Exporters once again were aggressive dollar sellers, keeping the won well-bid even as the main index of the local stock market fell 4.5%. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at KRW1,165.6 down from KRW1,170.6 Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar might have fallen even further if market players hadn't been concerned that the government might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the flagging U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Frank Gong, strategist at Bank of America in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears kept a bid under the dollar at around the KRW1,165 level, Gong said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Economy sold KRW700 billion worth of five-year \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  stabilization bonds Monday, leading players to conclude that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was imminent. The MOFE in the past has authorized the Bank of Korea to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  right after the issuance of such bonds, Gong said. \par \par \uc2  "Watch out for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the next two days," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Korean government is concerned about the won's appreciation - more than 14% against the dollar since mid-April - because of its negative impact on export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  More than half of the 49 companies surveyed by Korea's Ministry of Commerce, Industry and Energy said they won't be able to meet their export targets for the year at the current \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rate, according to a government report released Monday. \par \par \uc2  The baht finished modestly higher as market players digested the government's latest attempt to explain its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  The baht's recent appreciation to a two-year high against the dollar has fueled concerns among some exporters about the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength on their competitiveness in international markets. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asia the dollar was trading at 40.415 baht, down from THB40.490 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Commerce Minister Adisai Bodharamik expressed sympathy for exporters, saying a decline in the dollar below THB40 would hurt their competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  He said that even if the baht's appreciation against the dollar is in line with that of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region, such a rise would have a "psychological effect" on exporters. \par \par \uc2  Adisai's comments were in contrast with recent remarks by Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra who showed little concern about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength. \par \par \uc2  The baht hit its two-year high last week after Thaksin predicted the dollar would soon fall below THB40. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar tracked the yen lower in a listless session. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asia the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7352, up from S$1.7301 late Friday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar opened about even with its Friday close, but strengthened gradually throughout the day, mirroring its rise against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar finished a touch weaker in light trading. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar ended at NT$33.028 compared with NT$33.023 Friday. Trading ranged between NT$33.044 and NT$33.002. \par \par \uc2  The dollar overcame an early decline against the rupiah to finish higher after local companies boosted their dollar purchases for offshore debt repayments. \par \par \uc2  Near the end of trading the dollar was quoted at 8,810 rupiah, up from IDR8,000 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed unchanged against the peso at PHP50.380. \par \par \uc2  The resolution of a political stalemate helped boost sentiment toward the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Senator Robert Jaworski's announcement Sunday that he will support President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo effectively ended a deadlock in the battle for control of the Senate, which had threatened to paralyze the administration's economic reform program. \par \par \uc2  -By Alan Yonan Jr., Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4045; alan.yonan@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020722dy7m000jz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
