\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Directionless, local leads in focus. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 800 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 2002\par 12:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, June 3 (Reuters) - The Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  went \par \par \uc2  their own ways on Monday as uncertainty over the dollar/yen \par \par \uc2  direction following the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese \par \par \uc2  monetary authorities prompted the market to shift focuses to \par \par \uc2  local leads. \par \par \uc2      The dollar/yen recouped some lost ground after a \par \par \uc2  combination of factors -- the Japanese dollar-buying \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , strong economic data out of the U.S., and the \par \par \uc2  fact that the market is getting massively short of the dollar \par \par \uc2  -- gave it some tail winds. \par \par \uc2      Some dealers estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday alone \par \par \uc2  could have set the Bank of Japan back by around $10 billion. \par \par \uc2      Most players opted to stick to local factors and were \par \par \uc2  reluctant to buy aggressively into the dollar's strength \par \par \uc2  because they were unsure of its outlook. \par \par \uc2      "I don't think the trouble is over for the dollar by any \par \par \uc2  stretch. We still have to wait for mid-June corporate results \par \par \uc2  to come out, and I suspect that could hurt the dollar again," \par \par \uc2  said Claudio Piron, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered \par \par \uc2  in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "The problem is that the economic resilience in America has \par \par \uc2  not been translated into corporate resilience in term of \par \par \uc2  profitability," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar , which tends to track the yen \par \par \uc2  closer than other Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , came off. It \par \par \uc2  hovered around 1.7870 against 1.7850 late on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Indonsian rupiah , on the other hand, raked in \par \par \uc2  robust gains, rising to its nine-month high of 8,550 on the \par \par \uc2  back of buying from state banks and positive trade data. \par \par \uc2      Indonesia's trade surplus rose to $2.34 billion in April \par \par \uc2  from $2.22 billion in March and $2.20 billion in February. \par \par \uc2      The rupiah was barely affected by news the government \par \par \uc2  delayed, for the second time, a meeting on whether to proceed \par \par \uc2  with a planned auction of a 51 percent stake in \par \par \uc2  state-controlled Bank Niaga, primarily because the news broke \par \par \uc2  when the market was wrapping up for the day. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT FIRM \par \par \uc2  The baht was resilient, holding near its recent \par \par \uc2  highs due to support from equity inflows and increased optimism \par \par \uc2  about Thailand's economic outlook following encouraging April \par \par \uc2  data, especially the industrial production and exports growth. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded around 42.38 to the dollar from around \par \par \uc2  42.50 late on Friday. \par \par \uc2      Foreign investors continued to pour money into local \par \par \uc2  stocks. Last week alone, they bought a net 7.19 billion baht \par \par \uc2  ($169.75 million) worth of Thai shares. \par \par \uc2      May inflation eased to a 30-month low of 0.1 percent due \par \par \uc2  to \par \par \uc2  the declining cost of food, energy and cheap non-food \par \par \uc2  products, further fuelling speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \par \par \uc2  keep its benchmark rate unchanged at 2.00 percent later in the \par \par \uc2  day. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar closed at an 11-month high \par \par \uc2  despite repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on hefty \par \par \uc2  dollar offers from exporters. It finished at 34.139 to the \par \par \uc2  dollar, the highest close since mid-June last year. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said part of the reason the Taiwan \par \par \uc2  dollar was in demand was that it was seen as a cheap proxy for \par \par \uc2  long yen positions in option plays. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said they expected the Taiwan dollar's uptrend to \par \par \uc2  remain intact given the island's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2      Some suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should allow the \par \par \uc2  undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate instead of reining in its \par \par \uc2  gains to subsidise traditional industries. \par \par \uc2      "Taiwan has in fact amassed too much in foreign reserves, \par \par \uc2  thanks to the CBC's consistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Steve Xu, \par \par \uc2  regional economist at SG Research in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      "The most sensible policy response for the CBC now would be \par \par \uc2  to quickly fulfil market expectations of a stronger TWD by \par \par \uc2  allowing the USD/TWD to fall to 33.50. Otherwise, the CBC would \par \par \uc2  have to square off its long dollar positions at much worse \par \par \uc2  levels," he said in a report. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0820 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen   