\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE1-HK Exchange Fund assets HK$985.86 bln end-Oct. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carrie Lee \par \uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2001\par 07:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Nov 5 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) said on Monday the Exchange Fund had total assets of HK$985.86 billion (US$126.39 billion) at the end of October versus HK$992.23 billion at the end of September. \par \par \uc2  Exchange Fund data issued by the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed that during the 10 months from January to October the fund's investment income was HK$6.1 billion, reversing a HK$6.2 billion investment loss in the January-September period. \par \par \uc2  But after interest and expenses the fund made a net investment loss of HK$2.4 billion from January to October, versus a HK$13.9 billion loss in the January-September period. \par \par \uc2  Resources of the Exchange Fund are used to back the Hong Kong dollar, unless they are needed for general revenue. \par \par \uc2  Noting the investment income, HKMA Chief Executive Joseph Yam told legislators: "This was a positive return. We were not making a loss. We hope to be able to maintain that in the coming two months so that it won't be in the red at the year-end". \par \par \uc2  "But the conditions in financial markets are difficult to predict," he added, saying it was too early to predict if the fund would make a loss this year. \par \par \uc2  Last week, Yam said withdrawals of fiscal reserves from the Exchange Fund totalled HK$58 billion this financial year (April-March) to end-September. Yam said on Monday the government had made further withdrawals in October because of the fiscal deficit. \par \par \uc2  The fiscal deficit for the six months to end-September totalled HK$60.7 billion, a far cry from the HK$3 billion forecast in the fiscal 2001/02 budget unveiled in March. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong Financial Secretary Antony Leung said last month he would not rule out the deficit growing to HK$100 million. \par \par \uc2  Of the total Exchange Fund assets at end-October, HK$894.98 billion was foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets and HK$90.88 billion Hong Kong dollar assets. \par \par \uc2  The fund's accumulated surplus was HK$303.325 billion at end-October, versus HK$296.252 billion at end-September. The accumulated surplus fell HK$3.8 billion during the January-October period. \par \par \uc2  In the same 10 months, the fund made a loss of HK$37.8 billion on Hong Kong equities and an exchange loss of HK$8.9 billion, but those losses were more than offset by a HK$52.8 billion return on bonds. \par \par \uc2  At end-October, the Exchange Fund's \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  equities portfolio, largely amassed during a two-week market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August 1998 defending the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was worth HK$75.2 billion. \par \par \uc2  That included HK$49.3 billion slated for long term investment and HK$25.9 billion for future disposal through the sale of more Tracker Fund units. \par \par \uc2  The Tracker Fund was launched in November 1999 as a means of disposing of the governments stock portfolio, largely acquired during the controversial \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  As end-October, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  equity portfolio had earned income of HK$139.7 billion from disposal and dividends. \par \par \uc2  (US$1=HK$7.8). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011105dxb500cid\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
