\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Plot talk hits peso, Indonesia debt raises eyebrows. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Nick Edwards \par \uc2 1,215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2001\par 13:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      HONG KONG, Oct 26 (Reuters) - Talk of a plot to destabilise \par \par \uc2  the Philippine government and news of a planned U.S. dollar \par \par \uc2  bond deal from Indonesia's biggest bank were the key trading \par \par \uc2  points of an otherwise lacklustre Friday in Asian asset \par \par \uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2      Philippine President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo said rumours \par \par \uc2  of a plot against her government had undermined the peso \par \par \uc2  which fell past 52 to the dollar for the first time since \par \par \uc2  August 13 on Thursday and closed at 52.04 on Friday. \par \par \uc2      Most other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed in narrow ranges not far \par \par \uc2  from recent lows but a retreating U.S. dollar and the squaring \par \par \uc2  of long dollar positions ahead of the weekend pushed the \par \par \uc2  Singapore dollar off its three-month low and kept the \par \par \uc2  Thai baht off 10-week lows hit on Thursday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Japanese yen        climbed as high as 123.18 to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par greenback in Tokyo trade from 122.90/94 in New York, but eased\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par back to 122.57/62 in late trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Tokyo stocks reversed earlier gains after weak interim\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par results and a loss warning from Toshiba Corp fueled\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par worries about the performance at other high-tech firms, pushing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the benchmark Nikkei 225 down 0.78 percent to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10,795.16.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     COUP TALK HITS PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine peso was mired in coup talk on Friday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closing for the second day in a row below 52 pesos to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Why did it go down? Coup rumours," Arroyo told a news\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par conference.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The president's office has been battling for days to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par silence talk in local newspapers that a coup plot called "Black\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par October" was brewing in elements of the national police force.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The police and military spokesmen have repeatedly affirmed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par their loyalty to Arroyo.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Army spokesman Lieutenant Colonel Jose Mabanta said the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par army stood behind the president and would be watching for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par instability when she leaves for a state visit to Hong Kong and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par China at the weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par National security adviser Roilo Golez dismissed on Friday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par any threat to stability, saying an attempt to undermine the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government would be the result of people "fantasizing about\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par maybe getting back to power or eroding the credibility of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government".\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the talk has rattled the peso, already shaky from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par concerns about a yawning fiscal deficit likely to require\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par external financing, falling interest rates and a shrinking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade surplus.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In August, Arroyo urged the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to take necessary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par steps to strengthen the peso to at least 50 per dollar by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par end of the year.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said on Friday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the bank was not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par help the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STOCKS OUTPERFORM\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hong Kong stocks ended higher as Wall Street gains\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par triggered broad-based buying and sent airline Cathay Pacific\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  leaping 6.4 percent to just off its level of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par September 11.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Hang Seng Index        closed higher for the third\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par straight session, finishing up 1.6 percent at 10,404.74.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The index has gained six percent on the week but is still\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par down 31 percent this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Shares of Toshiba, Japan's top chipmaker, fell 4.67 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to 510 yen, helping to push down the benchmark Nikkei share\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par average by 84.94 points or 0.78 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The close was 2.32 percent off from Thursday's intraday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high of 11,052.01, its highest level since the September 11\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attacks in the United States sparked fears of global recession.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Singapore shares gave up almost all their gains to end flat\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on profit-taking ahead of the weekend, with the Straits Times\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Index ending up just 0.15 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Countering the overall market, the electronics index\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  jumped 3.37 percent, helped by the Nasdaq Composite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Index's 2.54 percent gain as well as post-results\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par relief at home.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par South Korea's KOSPI ended 0.23 percent higher,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par extending gains to a sixth session, helped by foreign buying in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par telecom shares on upbeat earnings forecasts.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Nasdaq's rally inspired a short squeeze in Taiwan, where\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the key TAIEX index ended 0.78 percent higher, its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par third successive firmer close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HSBC WINS MANDIRI DEBT MANDATE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HSBC confirmed market talk it had been appointed to explore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a dollar debt deal for PT Bank Mandiri which would mark the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par nation's first foray in the dollar debt market since the Asian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par financial crisis of 1997/98.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said the deal is expected to be small-sized with a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par five year tenor and will be seen as a benchmark of investor\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par confidence in President Megawati Sukarnoputri's government.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "With the Latin American risk coming off a bit, now is a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par good time as any to launch a bond. But I think they will have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to pay a good deal of premium," said a senior bond trader at a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S.-based investment bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia's credibility in the international capital market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has been battered after the spectacular collapse of Asia Pulp &\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Paper Co Ltd , a firm laden with $12.2 billion of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par debt, earlier this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The broader regional dollar bond market was quiet with most\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors adopting a cautious capital preservation strategy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par before the year-end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The market is very quiet and has a slightly weak tone. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors are probably weighing the impact of likely new\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par issues," said a senior bond dealer at a European investment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  1039 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     122.57       122.94         +0.30\par  Sing dlr      1.8282       1.8275         -0.04\par  Taiwan dlr     34.49        34.55         +0.16\par  Korean won   1296.30      1291.00         -0.41\par  Baht           44.84        44.75         -0.20\par  Peso           52.04        51.80         -0.46\par  Rupiah      10250.00     10220.00         -0.29\par  Ringgit       3.8000       3.7995         -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     122.57       114.45         -6.62\par  Sing dlr      1.8282       1.7365         -5.02\par  Taiwan dlr     34.49        32.90         -4.61\par  Korean won   1296.30      1277.00         -1.49\par  Baht           44.84        43.70         -2.54\par  Peso     