\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Asian Wall Street Journal - July 5. \b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2001\par 01:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 5 (Reuters) - The following stories were reported in Thursday's electronic version of The Asian Wall Street Journal: \par \par \uc2  * Sony may combine its Indian television channels with those of AOL Time Warner , making a potentially major realignment in one of Asia's largest television markets. \par \par \uc2  * A real-estate group with ties to Matsushita Electric has racked up more than $3 billion in debt and just reported its first loss. A finance expert has been brought in to clean up the mess. \par \par \uc2  * CyberWorks announced deeper-than-expected cuts for its Internet businesses, including the elimination of 40 percent of online jobs, and announced a bond issue to reduce interest payments. \par \par \uc2  * Cathay Pacific flights have begun to experience some delays from a go-slow campaign by pilots, but observers say \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's chief executive is hesitant to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  * China and Japan weren't able to resolve a three-month-old trade dispute during two days of talks and agreed to hold more talks later to limit the damage to their relationship. \par \par \uc2  * SK Telecom pushed back its launch of 3G mobile services by up to a year from the May 2002 target, joining a growing list of cautious operators world-wide. \par \par \uc2  * SingTel will invest $265 million over the next 18 months to open Internet data centers throughout Asia, a move that may challenge existing independent centers. \par \par \uc2  * The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will examine banks' larger \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions to ensure that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation isn't behind the peso's steep decline. \par \par \uc2  * Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left interest rates unchanged, indicating that its easing cycle is most likely over. The Reserve Bank of New Zealand also left rates alone. \par \par \uc2  * The value of Japan's merger-and-acquisition deals fell 65 percent in the first half, but closer inspection shows that asset shuffling may be rising, a study says. \par \par \uc2  * Asia Pulp & Paper's depositary receipts were suspended on the New York Stock Exchange as officials sought to delist them, saying they failed to meet minimum pricing criteria. \par \par \uc2  * Hutchison Whampoa got Europe's conditional clearance for its plan to take a stake in Europe's busiest container port, bolstering the company's presence in the container-handling business. \par \par \uc2  * Followers of the outlawed Falun Gong sect hanged themselves in a mass suicide at a prison camp, China and a human rights group said. But the sect claimed the inmates were tortured to death. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912dx740099l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
