\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Wall St shakes stocks, bonds await Argentina ripple. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Nick Edwards \par \uc2 1,198 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2001\par 12:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      HONG KONG, June 19 (Reuters) - Asian asset markets failed \par \par \uc2  to fight through Wall Street's gloom on Tuesday, with most \par \par \uc2  regional equity benchmarks flat to weaker and fixed income \par \par \uc2  markets trading nervously in the shadow cast by Argentina's \par \par \uc2  flailing economy. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A fall of two percent on Nasdaq\tab    kept Asian stocks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bowed, with only Hong Kong and Malaysia strong enough to break\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par decisively into positive territory, and weighed heavily on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sentiment for dollar bonds which saw spreads to risk-free U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Treasuries widen an average of 10 basis points on the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab   remained hostage to the fortunes of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan's yen which sank to one month lows against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar before recovering sharply in late trade after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Masaru Hayami said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was necessary if\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates move too rapidly.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Tokyo's Nikkei 225\tab    stock index wiped out earlier\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains to end lower for the third straight session, losing 0.97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent after concerns over the financial health of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par debt-strapped Japanese retailer Mycal Corp chilled\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ASIAN BOND SPREADS WIDEN\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Asian dollar bond spreads were wider across the board in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par thin trade with a fall on Wall Street undermining prices more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par than confusion over a change in Argentina's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Asian bonds have taken it on the chin since Nortel Networks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  warned of a $19.2 billion second quarter loss\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par last week sending U.S. corporate bond spreads sprawling and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pushing Asian investors to lock in profits on benchmark paper\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that has tightened an average of 30 basis points over the past\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par two weeks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Confusion over Argentina's introduction of a special\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exchange rate for exporters and importers sent emerging market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bond investors in New York scurrying for safety on Monday, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par near term fallout for Asian bonds were seen muted.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "This may make people realise that there are still risks in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the global financial system and people may re-evaluate some of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Asia," Brian Verlaan, head of Asian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fixed income research at Standard Chartered Bank in Singapore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "This will ultimately, coupled with some of the economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fundamentals in these countries, cause people to reassess\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par spreads, but I don't think there's an immediate knock-on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par effect," he told Reuters Television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The long end of the Philippine yield curve felt most\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressure with the country's 9.875 percent sovereign paper due\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in 2019 pushing out about five basis points (bps) at the open\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and moving 10-15 further out to be quoted at about 605 bps over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. Treasuries in late trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     At the shorter end Philippine '10s were about two bps wider\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at Asia's open, but had widened a further five bps in late\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade to around 497 bps over Treasuries, according to data from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters Fixed Income 3000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The sub-investment grade Philippines offers the most\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par representative comparison to Latin American risk and is the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par biggest Asian component in the benchmark EMBI, making the paper\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sensitive to moves in the index, dominated by Argentina.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO SLIDES\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso slid to five-month lows of 52.38 as corporates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par scrambled to buy the dollar on the weaker yen and concerns\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about the unsolved kidnappings in the southern Philippines.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "We'll take any excuse to buy the dollar. And we know the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can't afford to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with their small\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reserves," a local bank dealer said. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par international reserves stood at $14.44 billion at end-April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But others said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might take the opportunity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  given the market was heavily long of dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STOCKS REBOUND\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Hong Kong stocks found late support from a technical\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rebound after the oversold benchmark index hovered around the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 13,000 level for most of the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Hang Seng Index\tab   ended up 1.43 percent at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 13,133.66, helped by gains in the two biggest stocks HSBC\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Holdings and China Mobile .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Banking giant HSBC, which had fallen five percent in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par past month, rose 1.35 percent to HK$94, while China's biggest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par mobile phone operator jumped 3.32 percent to HK$40.40 after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shedding more than four percent on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par China shares also rebounded in late trade with the H-share\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  and the red chip indices mostly recovering\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par their respective two percent deficits to see H-shares end up\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par one percent and the red chips close just 0.30 percent lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIA BLAST FELLS RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par News of a bomb blast in Jakarta and another clash between\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par police and students protesting fuel price hikes dragged the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah to a two-week low of 11,385 per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Five people were wounded when a powerful bomb exploded at a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par boarding-house in a Jakarta suburb while police fired teargas\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to disperse 100 stone-throwing students near a university.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Jakarta said dollar profit-taking by interbank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players and some export-related inflows beyond 11,350 capped\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its downside. They said there was no sign of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but players were cautious a test of 11,400 may invite\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0958 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     122.83\tab  123.36\tab    +0.43\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8165\tab  1.8166\tab    +0.01\par  Taiwan dlr     34.37\tab   34.38\tab    +0.03\par  Korean won   1300.00\tab 1297.00\tab    -0.23\par  Baht\tab      45.23\tab   45.32\tab    +0.20\par  Peso\tab      52.29\tab   51.98\tab    -0.59\par  Rupiah\tab 11370.00     11280.00\tab    -0.79\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     122.83\tab  114.45\tab    -6.82\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8165\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.40\par  Taiwan dlr     34.37\tab   32.90\tab    -4.28\par  Korean wo