\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rangebound on yen,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2001\par 11:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 9 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were rangebound, not far from their recent lows on Monday, in the face of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threats and uncertainty about the near-term direction of the yen . \par \par \uc2  More warnings from Japanese officials against excessive exchange rate weakness kept the yen supported the firm side of 125 to the dollar for most of the day, making players wary of pushing the regionals lower. \par \par \uc2  But most analysts expected the dollar to move ahead again on continued safe haven flows after a brief period of consolidation. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is basically in a consolidation phase and there is some uncertainty on how long it will remain in this phase. So for the time being there is some respite for other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a chief dealer of a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  The rest of the region was also rife with talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as finance officials and politicians kept up their verbal routine. \par \par \uc2  Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were spotted selling dollars via onshore banks at around 1,343.00, continuing last week's aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, comments by Thai officials worked the other way, taking the baht to a new 37-month low. \par \par \uc2  The euro managed to hold its day highs around $0.9040 amid concerns over the U.S. economy after March payrolls data released on Friday showed the steepest monthly fall in ten years. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht perked up after rumours swirled in the market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 45.80-45.85. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said earlier it was monitoring the baht closely, but reiterated the baht weakness was caused by the soft yen and other external factors. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht fell to intraday lows of 45.85 partly due to a remark by Commerce Minister Adisai Bodharamik that a weak baht was helping exports. \par \par \uc2  "The market's interpretation of it was the government was willing to tolerate a weaker baht," said a Singapore dealer. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said Thailand had no plan to impose monetary controls to stem losses in the baht which hit fresh 37-month lows on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The one-month forward rate in the offshore market eased slightly to 30/60 satang per dollar from around 40/50 satang in the morning. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won moved within a tight range, helped by a steadier yen and on dollar selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Korea. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Seoul said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold an estimated $200 million via onshore banks at 1,342.0 won in the morning and 1,343.0 in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  But they scoffed at Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which came on the back of an aggressive $400-$500 million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week. \par \par \uc2  However, a bearish outlook for the region reinforced by weak U.S. March payrolls data and the KOSPI's fall following the Nasdaq's losses on Friday, kept sentiment depressed. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the market would keep an eye on more data from the U.S. including retail sales and the producer price index for March due later in the week. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar remained under selling pressure due to the regional trend and talk of a major local bank planning to buy a bank in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said players had bid up the dollar on reports that DBS Group , Southeast Asia's largest bank, was set to make a bid of up to HK$45 billion ($5.78 billion) for Hong Kong's Dao Heng Bank . \par \par \uc2  Otherwise, the market was awaiting flash data on January-March growth and the government's revised 2001 growth forecast to be released on Tuesday. Economists polled by Reuters expected the economy to grow 5.9 percent in the first quarter. \par \par \uc2  "The official 2001 economic growth forecast - currently at 5-7 percent - is expected to be revised downwards," said a DBS report. \par \par \uc2  "However, this should not have any material impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and equity markets which have largely priced in the slower growth," it said. \par \par \uc2  The Reuters poll produced an average forecast of 4.6 percent growth in 2001. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was wedged in a narrow range, with foreign banks trimming long dollar positions and state banks buying the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  One Jakarta dealer said Bank Indonesia, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was heard entering the market to sell a small amount of dollar at 10,850. \par \par \uc2  The market expected a long-awaited visit by the IMF to Indonesia this week would give the ailing rupiah some reprieve. \par \par \uc2  The visit should pave the way for disbursement of a $400 million loan delayed by the IMF since late last year and trigger a $5.8 billion debt rescheduling deal with the Paris Club of official creditors. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was trapped within a tight range on U.S. dollar selling by players wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  said exporters sold U.S. dollars as the Taiwan dollar eased towards its session low of 32.95 fearing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to test the 33 level. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped the Taiwan dollar's gains at 32.90, leaving it confined to a narrow range. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Perng Fai-nan said on Monday the Taiwan dollar rate should reflect changes in the international financial environment. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said sentiment was weighed by a fall in the TAIEX and the continued deadlock between China and the U.S. over a spy plane and its crew detained by Beijing. \par \par \uc2  The market will be watching for March trade balance data due on Tuesday. A Reuters poll showed an average of $759 million surplus expected for March, compared with a surplus of $1.059 billion in February. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was steady with only a few small offshore deals reported as markets in Manila were closed for the Valour Day holiday. Trade will resume on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said a weak outlook for the yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to keep the peso pressured as exporters and overseas workers held back dollars. \par \par \uc2  Importers would also be seeking U.S. dollars because of a shorter week with Philippine markets again closed on Thursday and Friday for the Easter break. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0932 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Pre