\par\par \b \uc2  HKMA Outlines Flexible Approach To HKD Strengthening \b0\par\par\uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2000\par 13:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG -(Dow Jones)- The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday outlined the circumstances under which it operates in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when the Hong Kong dollar is strengthening. \par \par \uc2  According to the Exchange Fund Advisory Subcommittee on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , chaired by the HKMA Chief Executive Joseph Yam, the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should remain flexible in dealing with a strengthening Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  It said the "complex interaction of a number of different circumstances" that can trigger the selling of U.S. dollars to the HKMA - in exchange for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars - "precludes" applying specific rules for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop a rise in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In deciding when to act the HKMA should take account of the size of the gap between the market rate for the U.S. dollar and the HK$7.80 convertibility rate, the difference between Hong Kong dollar and U.S. dollar interest rates, and the level of the aggregate balance. \par \par \uc2  The convertibility rate is the rate at which it guarantees to buy Hong Kong dollars from the market, thereby putting a ceiling on any rise in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But when the U.S. dollar is under selling pressure and the banks come to the HKMA, the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can then either reject any bank's offer to sell it U.S. dollars, accept it, or "adopt a more active approach in purchasing U.S. dollars", in efforts to restore the liquidity in the aggregate balance. \par \par \uc2  The aggregate balance, a key measure of interbank liquidity, amounts to the balance of funds in clearing accounts maintained by the banks with the HKMA, and is an important feature of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system that pegs the Hong Kong dollar to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  If the HKMA buys U.S. dollars from the banks, it then credits the aggregate balance with the funds. \par \par \uc2  EFAC stressed the "dangers" of injecting liquidity into the aggregate balance too quickly when it has dipped into a deficit, thereby giving rise to concern the HKMA is interfering with the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Conversely, EFAC also said acting too slowly to restore funds in the\par balance can lead to unnecessarily large fluctuations in the exchange\par rate and interest rates.\par - - 28/09/00 11-04G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par When the aggregate balance is in deficit due to Hong Kong dollar\par selling, the lack of liquidity will force interbank interest rates up to\par a point that will then spark buying of the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and an\par eventual restoration of funds to the system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Last month, Hong Kong's quasi-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rejected calls for\par so-called two-way convertibility, that is, a guaranteed exchange rate\par for the Hong Kong dollar both when the U.S. dollar rises or falls.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EFAC cited the speculative buying of the Hong Kong dollars, or\par significant non-speculative buying, as two of the "circumstances"\par against the introduction of two-way convertibility. It also cited a\par sharp decline in the aggregate balance arising from a speculative\par outflow of funds or large commercial selling orders of Hong Kong\par dollars.\par -0- 28/09/00 11-21G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw9s04oaz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
