\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-HK Exchange Fund total assets fall 4.7 pct in 1H. \b0\par\par\uc2 569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 2000\par 12:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, July 31 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) said on Monday the total assets of the Exchange Fund, which backs the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fell HK$48 billion in the first half of 2000 to HK$966.4 billion at the end of June. \par \par \uc2  Liabilities totalled HK$680.4 billion, down from HK$723 billion at the end of December 1999, the HKMA said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  The accumulated surplus of the Exchange Fund, was HK$285.9 billion at the end of June, down from HK$291.3 billion at end-December, due to lower Hong Kong equity prices. \par \par \uc2  "The decrease in the accumulated surplus was caused by the significant fall in the prices of Hong Kong stocks held by the Exchange Fund during the period," the HKMA said. \par \par \uc2  "There was an evaluation loss of HK$24 billion in the Exchange Fund's equity portfolio, which more than offset the investment gains in bonds and other financial instruments held by the fund." \par \par \uc2  The market value of equity investments in the government's Hong Kong equity portfolio was HK$170.905 billion at end-June versus HK$218.806 billion at end-December, the HKMA said. \par \par \uc2  During the first half, a total of HK$23.593 billion of shares was sold under the tap facility of the Tracker Fund . \par \par \uc2  The government bought HK$118.1 billion worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  stocks in a controversial market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August 1998, and disposed of HK$36.7 billion via Tracker Fund unit trusts last year. \par \par \uc2  TOTAL ASSETS FALL 4.6 PCT \par \par \uc2  The HKMA said the main reason for the decrease in the total assets of the Exchange Fund were: \par \par \uc2  * HK$22.1 billion redemption of bank notes issued at the end of 1999 to cope with Y2K-related demand \par \par \uc2  * HK$16.1 billion fall in placements by other institutions including placements from other statutory bodies and bank borrowings \par \par \uc2  * unwinding of Y2K contingency held by banks with the HKMA \par \par \uc2  * HK$5.4 billion fall in accumulated surplus. \par \par \uc2  "Concerns in developed economies, particularly the U.S., over inflation have led to very high volatility in financial markets, including the Hong Kong equity market, and the performance of the Exchange Fund in the first half of 2000 has been adversely affected by the net fall in the prices of Hong Kong equities during the period," said HKMA Chief Executive Joseph Yam in a statement. \par \par \uc2  The losses in the first half were largely recouped as the Hang Seng Index rallied by over 1,000 points in the first three weeks of July, Yam said, but also noted that the index had fallen by around 780 points since. \par \par \uc2  "Until the outlook for interest rates become clearer the investment environment for the rest of the year will remain uncertain and we can expect to see more ups and downs of this kind," he said. \par \par \uc2  The HK$966.4 billion total assets figure include assets held by the Exchange Fund's subsidiaries such as the Hong Kong Mortgage Corp. \par \par \uc2  Excluding subsidiaries, the Exchange Fund's assets stood at HK$956.1 billion at the end of June, up HK$21.7 billion from end-May, the HKMA said in a separate statement on Monday. \par \par \uc2  ((Tiffany Wu, Hong Kong Newsroom +852 2843-6519, Fax +852 2845-0636 hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw7v00vyx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
