\par\par \b \uc2  China Bonds End Higher On Weaker Stocks; Yuan Slips \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2000\par 10:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- China's government bond prices closed higher Thursday in active trade, as investors flocked to fixed-income instruments amid continued weakness among local shares, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar resumed its climb after a one-day breather, ending at 8.2792 yuan from Wednesday's CNY8.2786 as importers came back into the market to buy more dollars. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit an intraday high of CNY8.2882, which traders considered a market aberration. Trading immediately went back to the normal range without \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar slipped to CNY1.0513 from CNY1.0613 in the last session, while the yen rose to CNY7.8711 per 100 yen from Wednesday's CNY7.7950. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan can only be converted on current account or trade transactions. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading is tightly regulated, making speculation virtually impossible. \par \par \uc2  The bond market was rejuvenated as funds flowed back from the equity market, which is currently mired in consolidation. \par \par \uc2  "This makes the market liquidity back to normal level," a trader at Shenyin & Wanguo Securities in Shanghai said. \par \par \uc2  Due to the lack of any other investment tools, the local stock and bond markets usually move in opposite directions. \par \par \uc2  The new 10-year floating-rate bond gained CNY0.20 to CNY101.94 on trade of 475,511 lots, leading to an annual yield of 1.04% compared with 1.26% Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The 1999 10-year bond rose CNY0.07 to CNY101.46 on trade of 393,690 lots, with its effective yield edging down to 3.44% from Wednesday's 3.45%. \par \par \uc2  Trading volume went up to CNY1.49 billion Thursday, as compared with CNY1.09 billion Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  China's bond market is off-limits to foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  -By Ramoncito dela Cruz, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6248-3268; ramoncito.delacruz@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7603aor\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
