\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 : Ctrl Bk Knocks Won Off Post-Crisis High \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 673 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 2000\par 10:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- Aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  forced the South Korean won down steeply during Asian trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealing in other regional markets was generally quieter, although both the Philippine peso and the Indonesian rupiah were sold down to test the bottom of their recent ranges. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came soon after the start of trading in Seoul, which had seen the won bid up to a fresh post-crisis high, with the dollar sold down to a low of KRW1,104.10, its lowest level since late November 1997. \par \par \uc2  Dealers estimated that the authorities purchased between $500 million and $750 million, driving the dollar sharply higher to KRW1,116.90, its highest level in nearly two weeks. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action came hard on the heels of the bank of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen, and was widely assumed by market players to be aimed at restoring the won's competitiveness relative to the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The specific motivation for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today was the March trade numbers," said Graham Courtney, regional economist at Warburg Dillon Read in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Data released over the weekend revealed a pronounced narrowing of Korea's trade surplus, which dropped to just $382 million in March compared with $2.35 billion in the same month last year. \par \par \uc2  Courtney blamed the decline largely on a deterioration in Korea's terms of trade, saying that the authorities in Seoul are anxious to enhance export competitiveness while imported inflation remains subdued. \par \par \uc2  "As long as the terms of trade are bad, I think the government will err on the side of an undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  Other analysts, however, argued that the BOK's action, which was backed up by verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Finance Ministry, was impelled more by domestic considerations ahead of next week's National Assembly elections. \par \par \uc2  "Won appreciation equals a de facto monetary tightening, which is a negative for the equity market: something the government wants to avoid so close to election," said Steven Xu, regional treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  By the end of the Seoul session the dollar had eased slightly to trade at KRW1,112.30, down from its earlier high but up from KRW1,106.00 at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  In other regional markets the Philippine peso dropped to its lowest level in six months during intraday trading as deteriorating sentiment toward the political outlook spurred dollar buying in the wake of weekend rumors of a possible coup attempt aimed at unseating President Estrada. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise against the peso was capped at PHP41.185, however, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  threatened to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local unit. \par \par \uc2  By the close the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had retreated to PHP41.135, the same level as Friday's close, prompting some dealers to suggest that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have covertly sold dollars. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah also dropped to its lowest level in six months, as the dollar broke up through resistance at IDR7,650 to hit a high of IDR7,690. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains were largely driven by corporate demand for dollars in thin market conditions ahead of Tuesday's and Thursday's Indonesian holidays. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asia, the dollar was quoted at IDR7,685, up from IDR7,615 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Markets in Singapore and Thailand were relatively quiet. Against the Singapore dollar the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped to S$1.7142 from S$1.7181 late Friday. Against the baht, the dollar eased to THB37.780 from THB37.920. \par \par \uc2  With markets in Taipei closed Monday and Tuesday for a holiday, there was no dealing in the New Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  SUBSCRIBERS CAN FIND ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  COMMENT ON: \par \par \uc2  TELERATE PAGES [1136] OR [4250] \par \par \uc2  DOW JONES NEWSWIRES BY SEARCHING THE CODE N/FXW \par \par \uc2  BLOOMBERG BY ENTERING NI FRX \par \par \uc2  REUTERS BY ENTERING CODE \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /DJ \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw4301q9x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
