\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 :Mostly Up;Verbal  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Checks Won \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 690 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 09:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  finished local trading hours Tuesday a touch stronger against the U.S. dollar, but activity was relatively subdued and regional markets generally trendless. \par \par \uc2  Enthusiastic buying of the won by foreign equity investors lifted the Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  steeply in early trading. Within an hour of the open, heavy dollar sales had pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an intraday low of 1,115.10 won, only just above its 13-month low of KRW1,114.00 hit last month. \par \par \uc2  The speed of the won's run-up proved uncomfortably fast for the Korean monetary authorities, prompting an official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Economy to declare that the government will not tolerate further strengthening in the won. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the Bank of Korea warned that the won's appreciation could damage the country's economy and said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to act to stabilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , coupled with government-backed dollar buying by the state-run Korea Development Bank, pushed the won back down from its high, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  still ended up on the day. \par \par \uc2  At the close the dollar was quoted at KRW1,118.50, down from KRW1,119.20 Monday. \par \par \uc2  Although Korean officials have said the government is ready to issue further tranches of won-denominated bonds to fund future \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , most market participants remain confident that the won will continue to strengthen over time. \par \par \uc2  Rather than attempting to reverse the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's upward trend, the authorities are merely trying to limit its appreciation to a manageable pace, they believe. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in the region the New Taiwan dollar ended little changed, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought U.S. dollars to counter the upward pressure on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from continued foreign fund inflows. \par \par \uc2  Despite a heightening of tensions with mainland China in the run-up to Taiwan's March 18 presidential election, offshore market players argue that the island's favorable economic fundamentals will support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the long term. In the short term the authorities in Taipei will act to smooth any excessive market volatility, they add. \par \par \uc2  At the end of local trading, the U.S. dollar was quoted against the Taiwanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at NT$30.762, little changed from NT$30.764 the previous day. \par \par \uc2  In Southeast Asia the Philippine peso ended sharply lower as the local equity market index dropped 3%. The fall reflected the damage inflicted on investor confidence by an ongoing price manipulation scandal on the Manila stock exchange, which Tuesday triggered the mass resignation of the bourse's compliance staff. \par \par \uc2  By the close of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing, the dollar had risen to 40.980 pesos, up from PHP40.900 Monday. Dealers widely expect the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to breach the PHP41.00 mark Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar recovered slightly from recent lows, after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to sustain its advance above S$1.7250. Some dealers suspected the local \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold U.S. dollars to bring the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back into line with its target index. \par \par \uc2  Toward the end of trading in Asia, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7213, down from S$1.7252 the day before. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht also gained ground, with the U.S. dollar easing back to 38.0250 baht late in Asia, from THB38.1250 the previous day. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah ended Asian dealing a fraction weaker after reports that Indonesian president Abdurrahman Wahid had canceled meetings for a cardiac checkup raised fresh fears about the head of state's fragile health. A presidential spokesman denied the medical was unscheduled. \par \par \uc2  Towards the end of Asian dealing the dollar was trading at 7,455 rupiah, compared with IDR7,447 the day before. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  SUBSCRIBERS CAN FIND ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  COMMENT ON: \par \par \uc2  TELERATE PAGES [1136] OR [4250] \par \par \uc2  DOW JONES NEWSWIRES BY SEARCHING THE CODE N/FXW \par \par \uc2  BLOOMBERG BY ENTERING NI FRX \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par REUTERS BY ENTERING CODE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 /DJ\par -0- 07/03/00 09-07G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw370195q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
