\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Mostly easier, volumes shrink. \b0\par\par\uc2 782 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 1999\par 09:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Dec 27 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly \par \par \uc2  easier in late Monday trade, with activity dominated by \par \par \uc2  position squaring and commercial flows in thin, end-year \par \par \uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2      Holidays in Sydney and \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dampened interest further. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen\tab     crept higher despite repeated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par warnings from Japanese officials and the Bank of Japan's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par decision to leave a record 4.5 trillion yen surplus in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par money market in its determination to keep overnight rates near\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par zero amid any build-up in Y2K pressures.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Warnings against further yen strength were somewhat\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par countered by BOJ governor Masaru Hayami's comment that the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen's rise relected increased overseas confidence in Japan's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A smattering of dollar sales by exporters and dollar bids\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by state-run Korea Development Bank helped confine dollar/won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to a tight trading range, with dealers expecting the mood to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remain quiet until the new year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But bullishness over the won persisted despite incessant\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par verbal and direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent weeks, with traders\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expecting an appetite for stocks to push the won above 1,110 in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the first quarter of next year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it expected gross domestic product\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par growth to come in at 10.02 percent this year, compared with its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par earlier forecast of 8.8 percent growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It also cut its 2000 inflation forecast to 3.1 percent from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par an earlier 3.8 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar bounced to a 25-month closing high,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bolstered by active foreign inflows to the stock market and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollar sales by exporters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Taipei shares gained 2.4 percent in a brisk rally fuelled\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by longer-term investors, especially foreign funds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The cabinet said Taiwan's surplus should hit US$11.5-12\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion in 1999, exceeding the finance ministry's latest $10.5\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion forecast.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Taiwan's index of leading indicators showed a healthy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "green" light for a second straight month, showing the effects\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of a massive September earthquake had all but subsided.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Trade in the rupiah was extremely thin with year-end\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par activity further slowed by concerns over Y2K.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Jakarta said they expected it to hover around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the 7,000 per dollar level until the end of the year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market seemed to have shrugged off news of more clashes\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par between Christians and Moslems in Ambon at the weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     More than 700 people have died since Moslem-Christian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bloodshed erupted in the Moluccas last January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was easier, in line with the baht, with trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par largely driven by commercial transactions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A Reuters poll showed the country's GDP was expected to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par grow an average 2.94 percent in 1999 and 3.97 percent in 2000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par compared with government predictions for 3.0 to 3.5 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par growth in 1999 and 4.0 to 5.0 percent in 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The economy contracted 0.5 percent in 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar was barely moved but dealers said it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remained well supported by a bullish stock market and further\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par evidence of a pick-up in domestic growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Singapore's total manufacturing output rose 18.2 percent in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par November compared with the same month of 1998. The electronics\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sector grew 25.5 percent year-on-year in November.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht was slightly lower in a paper thin market as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par importers bought dollars to pay their bills.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said gains in the local stock market barely boosted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because it was driven mostly by retail investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and not foreign institutions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht is expected to move in a narrow 37.65-38.00 range\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this week.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0814 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     102.56\tab  102.55\tab    -0.01\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6680\tab  1.6680\tab    +0.00\par  Taiwan dlr     31.53\tab   31.57\tab    +0.14\par  Korean won   1133.50\tab 1131.30\tab    -0.19\par  Baht\tab      37.65\tab   37.55\tab    -0.27\par  Peso\tab      40.22\tab   40.10\tab    -0.30\par  Rupiah\tab  6980.00\tab 6980.00\tab    +0.00\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.8000\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     102.56\tab  113.20\tab   +10.37\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6680\tab  1.6495\tab    -1.11\par  Taiwan dlr     31.53\tab   32.17\tab    +2.05\par  Korean won   1133.50\tab 1200.00\tab    +5.87\par  Baht\tab      37.65\tab   36.20\tab    -3.85\par  Peso\tab      40.22\tab   38.75\tab    -3.65\par  Rupiah\tab  6980.00\tab 7800.00\tab   +11.75\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7999\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ((Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Desk (65) 870-3087\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par email:asia.\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 @reuters.com)).\