\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 : Won Forced Down, Late Buying Lifts Baht \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 686 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 1999\par 09:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  coupled with government-directed dollar buying forced the South Korean won lower for the second day running on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In Southeast Asia, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  drifted sideways for most of the session, before a flurry of late dollar sales by market participants based in Europe pushed the Thai baht and the Indonesian rupiah up sharply to end the day higher. \par \par \uc2  The Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Economy sought to set its stamp on the day's trading in Seoul by issuing a statement minutes before the local market's open, declaring that "the won's appreciation is never desirable." \par \par \uc2  In recent days, the monetary authorities in Seoul have struggled to check a rapid appreciation of the won, driven by heavy trade and investment flows. \par \par \uc2  After the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the market Tuesday, Wednesday's verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was backed up by dollar-purchases executed by the state-run Korea Development Bank. \par \par \uc2  By the end of local trading in Seoul, the dollar had been driven up to close at KRW1,135.00, well above KRW1,133.30 at the end of Tuesday's session. \par \par \uc2  Despite the dollar's advance against the won Wednesday, the majority of market participants retained their bullish view on the Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . U.S.-based J.P. Morgan, for example, was sticking to its year-end exchange rate forecast of KRW1,100. \par \par \uc2  "That's a very aggressive target," conceded Chia Hsin-Li, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at the bank. \par \par \uc2  "But in the long run, the equity inflow story is still there and is still strong," she added, saying that Wednesday's selloff in Korean stocks, which saw Seoul's benchmark index plunge by nearly 4%, was due to profit-taking by local players and not to any change of heart by foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  The won is also being supported by South Korea's strong trade position. Over the first 11 months of the year, the country notched up a trade surplus of $21.6 billion, the Korean customs service announced Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in North Asia, the new Taiwan dollar closed marginally weaker, with the U.S. dollar edging higher to close at NT$31.640, compared with NT$31.637 at the end of Tuesday's session. \par \par \uc2  In Southeast Asia, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  drifted sideways for most of the day before a late flurry of buying briefly lifted the baht and the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "We saw some (dollar) selling when Europe opened," explained one Singapore based broker, saying that market players in London had sold the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against baht, rupiah and Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  "But these are very thin markets and there are no big amounts going through. This was just some (dollar) longs selling to take profits and square off their positions before the end of the year," he said. \par \par \uc2  By the time Asian trading ended, the dollar had lifted a little from its earlier low against the baht of THB38.4300 to trade at THB38.4650. Late Tuesday, the dollar had been quoted at THB38.5550. \par \par \uc2  Dealing was unaffected by the no-confidence debate in the Thai parliament, with most traders assured the government will survive unscathed. \par \par \uc2  News that the International Monetary Fund assistance program to Indonesia suspended in August will be superseded by a new extended program to run until November 2003 had no impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealings in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  Late in the Asian day, the dollar was quoted against the rupiah at IDR7,202, down from IDR7,235 the day before. \par \par \uc2  Against the Singapore dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at S$1.6790, flat compared with S$1.6787 the day before. \par \par \uc2  In Manila, the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to raise its overnight lending rate to 12% from 11% in anticipation of increased funding demands over the new year had little effect on peso trading. \par \par \uc2  On the Philippine Dealing System, the dollar closed against the peso at PHP40.690, up from PHP40.665 the day before. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvcf08e2y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
