\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 ; Won Forced Lower By Govt  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 532 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 1999\par 09:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  forced the South Korean won lower Tuesday, but for the most part Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to track sideways against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  In Seoul, the South Korean finance ministry backed up another round of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with dollar purchases executed directly by the Bank of Korea and indirectly through the Korea Development Bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers estimated that the authorities bought in excess of $200 million, lifting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to close at 1,133.30 won, up from KRW1,128.20 at the end of Monday's session. \par \par \uc2  Despite Tuesday's action, market players retained their view that the won will still strengthen over the medium term. \par \par \uc2  Economists pointed out that over the long run the South Korean government is unlikely to continue buying dollars in opposition to market forces and economic fundamentals. By issuing stabilization bills carrying a coupon of 6.97% to fund the purchase of dollars returning a yield of 6.20% or less, the authorities face heavy costs in mounting \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the won down, they noted. \par \par \uc2  However, few observers doubted that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue in the short term. Some suggested the Seoul authorities have drawn a line in the sand at last week's two-year dollar low of KRW1,125, which they appear determined to hold at least until the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  In other regional markets, the New Taiwan dollar closed lower as market players sold to exit long positions in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  At the Taipei close, the U.S. dollar was quoted at NT$31.637, up from NT$32.620 the previous day. \par \par \uc2  In Southeast Asia, the Indonesian rupiah failed to respond to a clutch of positive developments, including news of pending investments in Indonesian companies by U.S. institutions. \par \par \uc2  With markets in Jakarta quiet during the Islamic fasting month of Ramadan and with many credit lines cut ahead of the New Year by overseas banks, there was little interest to trade the rupiah, which drifted sideways through Asian hours. \par \par \uc2  Toward the end of local dealing, the U.S. dollar was quoted against the rupiah at IDR7,235, compared with IDR7,227 the day before. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht finished a touch stronger, but still well within recent ranges, as the dollar eased to THB38.5550 toward the end of Asian trading, down from THB38.5950 the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Against the Singapore dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended the Asian day at S$1.6787, little changed from S$1.6791 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the Philippine Dealing System, the peso edged higher against the dollar after Finance Secretary Edgardo Espiritu said the government will reduce its deficit during December. \par \par \uc2  Over the first 11 months of the year, the Philippines' budget deficit rose to 110.15 billion pesos, well in excess of the government's PHP101 billion target for the whole year. \par \par \uc2  At the close of local dealing, the U.S. dollar had slipped to PHP40.690, down from PHP40.705 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvce08h4c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
