\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Mkts: Rates, Forwards Up Late;Demand, Tracker Fund \b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1999\par 10:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG -(Dow Jones)- Hong Kong interbank rates and forward premiums continued to strengthen late Thursday, with traders citing overseas demand for short-end Hong Kong dollar forwards and local preparations for the sale of the government's Tracker share fund. \par \par \uc2  Forward premiums of all maturities opened higher Thursday and continued to climb throughout the session. The one-month premium is 40-45 points above the spot rate from 35-40 late Wednesday, while the one-year is at 660-670 from 630-650. \par \par \uc2  Traders cited a number of reasons behind the move, including interest from London overnight, where players bought into the one-month in an effort to cover their short positions. \par \par \uc2  However, a dealer from a British bank said the interest rate squeeze may reflect typical end-of-month demand. \par \par \uc2  Another trader with a local bank said banks were preparing for the release of the government's HK$10 billion Hang Seng Index-tracking mutual fund by storing up liquidity, as they were unsure how much demand for the fund will drain cash from the banking system. \par \par \uc2  "They don't want to lend in the one- to three-month period," he said. "And that is affecting interest rates." \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate rose to 6.25% from 5.88% late Wednesday, while the one-month is also higher at 6.06% from 5.83%. Three-month money was only slightly higher though, at 6.69% from 6.53%. \par \par \uc2  The local bank trader said he expected rates to peak early next week - probably around their current level - ahead of the close of the Tracker Fund initial public offering Nov. 4. \par \par \uc2  The market is confident the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if rates go beyond this level by injecting liquidity into the banking system, he said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the Hong Kong dollar is trading stronger, as the overnight Hibor rose about one percentage point higher than the comparable U.S. rate, encouraging some arbitraging. Some "light" U.S. dollar selling pushed the spot rate stronger to HK$7.7703 to the U.S. dollar from HK$7.7709 earlier Thursday, and further below the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's convertibility rate of HK$7.7711. Late Wednesday the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at HK$7.7705. \par \par \uc2  However the British dealer said he expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bottom at HK$7.7700 due to limited interest in further U.S. dollar selling. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the government paper market, the benchmark 10-year Exchange Fund\par note was quoted at 99.45, with a yield-to maturity of 7.5%.\par                  Latest        Late Wednesday\par Overnight Hibor   6.25%           5.88%\par 1-mo Hibor        6.06%           5.83%\par 3-mo Hibor        6.69%           6.53%\par USD/HKD Spot   HK$7.7703       HK$7.7705\par 6-mo HKD Fwd    240-250         210-220\par 1-yr HKD Fwd    660-670         630-650\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - by Liz Rudall; (852) 2802-7002; elizabeth.rudall@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1053 4178 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvas07mfa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
