\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  firm, Wall Street soothes. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Tamora Vidaillet \par \uc2 1,001 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 1999\par 11:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Oct 25 (Reuters) - Asian stock markets were mixed \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Monday, with Hong Kong\tab    , Singapore\tab     and Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2     partly lifted by rises on Wall Street. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Elsewhere, Korean stocks\tab      ended 2.5 percent lower on\par jitters over how much of Daewoo Group's\tab \tab  debts would\par have to be written off while Manila stocks\tab     fell to an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par eight-month low over rising interest rates and prospects of weak\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporate earnings.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Most regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  made some headway, and analysts\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said further gains were likely over the longer term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are in a consolidative phase and that's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about to end. We now expect Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to start\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strengthening from here," said Chin Loo Thio, strategist at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Paribas.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HANG SENG CLIMBS, RESPONSE TO TRACKER FUND MUTED\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hong Kong stocks climbed more than two percent at one stage\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but that was spurred more by Wall Street's strong performance on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday and activity surrounding particular blue-chips than by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par any reaction to the government's marketing of its unit trust.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government launched its much awaited Tracker Fund at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par midday to help sell down a massive stock portfolio amassed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par during its August market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Some analysts in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the size and terms of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par blue-chip fund were largely within market expectations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The fund totals HK$10 billion and includes shares of all 33\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par index companies.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Retail investors are expected to be given a minimum discount\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of five percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BAHT PIERCES KEY RESISTANCE BUT DOLLAR BULLS LURK\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht\tab     regained the most ground in off-shore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade, with domestic financial markets closed for a holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts in Singapore said it was taking cue from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par generally firmer regional tone as well as from renewed strength\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the rupiah\tab    .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Intra-day, dollar/baht slipped as U.S. banks sold dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but they came up against some bids from European funds around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the 38.90/95 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers said dollar demand was likely to prevail later\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the week, and the baht could head back towards 39.40.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "We have seen dollar/Thai under some downward pressure in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the last few days...associated with the better picture in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia," David Simmonds, regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Citibank, told Reuters Television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     RUPIAH STICKS ON CABINET QUESTION-MARK\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah stuck to levels of around 6,800 per dollar as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors took a wait-and-see stance towards the appointment of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a new post-election cabinet.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders in Indonesia said they generally see Thursday as the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par day President Abdurrahman Wahid will announce his new line-up.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "For the rupiah, much of the profoundly good political news\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of last week is rather fully priced in. Markets are generally\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short U.S. dollar, long rupiah with no rush to square those\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions," Simmonds said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If we are to see a stronger rupiah over the next few days,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par one has got to look for new trigger points like the formation of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a new cabinet. We're looking for a reasonable market-friendly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outcome there," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par President Wahid said at the weekend that he might take on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ministers from previous cabinets, but insisted they would have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to be honest and follow the new government's plans to promote\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic development.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Syahril Sabirin said on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monday that he saw the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthening to 6,000 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar at most.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR SEEN FAVOURED LONG-TERM\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With the relative lack of liquidity in most regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the moment, analysts said the Singapore dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  was seeing renewed interest.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The market is liquid, with dollar/Sing enjoying quite a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bit of inflows. It's much better than the baht at the moment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after the Bank of Thailand enforced swap restrictions," said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thio of Paribas.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Investors were eyeing the country's steady recovery from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the economic downturn, with inflation data released at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weekend showing the consumer price index (CPI) back near\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pre-crisis levels.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CPI rose 1.2 percent in the year to September, compared with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a 0.9 percent year-on-year rise in August.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000.........0.01%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Rupiah......6805.00......6850.00.........0.66%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Baht..........38.88........39.14.........0.67%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Peso..........40.08........40.17.........0.24%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Sing dlr.....1.6636.......1.6678.........0.25%