\par\par \b \uc2  US/HK forwards, interbank rates open easier. \b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 1999\par 05:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab \tab  Open\tab     Previous Close\par  HK$ SPOT\tab \tab     7.7655/60\tab    7.7655/57\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  FORWARDS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Three-month\tab \tab  180-190\tab     193-198\par  Six-month\tab \tab    475-495\tab     490-510\par  One-year\tab \tab 1,090-1,120\tab 1,100-1,140\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  INTERBANK RATE (IN PERCENTAGE)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Overnight\tab \tab  5.56-5.75\tab   5.37-5.62\par  Three-month\tab      6.25-6.50\tab   6.25-6.50\par  Six-month\tab \tab  6.94-7.19\tab   7.06-7.25\par  One-year\tab \tab   7.25-7.50\tab   7.31-7.56.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Sept 7 (Reuters) - US/HK forwards and Hong Kong interbank rates opened slightly easier on Tuesday, despite the settlement of a decline of HK$155 million in the aggregate balance of the banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) forecast the balance before the discount window opened on Tuesday to be HK$748 million.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After markets closed on Monday, the HKMA announced several measures to ensure adequate banking liquidity for the turn of the millennium.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The HKMA said it would enlarge the discount window from November 15 to January 31 2000 by allowing certain instruments such as triple-A rated securities to be used as collateral, and launch term repurchase agreement facilities (repos) from December 1 1999 to January 31 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The move was the first loosening of collateral requirements on discount window borowings since the HKMA ruled last year that no new issues of debt securities other than Exchange Fund bills and notes would be accepted as collateral at its discount window.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the effect of the new measures would not be seen until closer to year-end, but they expected less upward pressure on interbank rates as a result of improved liquidity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A dealer said the measures would not affect the direction of interbank rates, though the spread between interbank rates and Exchange Fund bills and notes could narrow.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said Exchange Fund bills and notes were in higher demand because some banks had thought they would be needed as collateral to borrow from the discount window ahead of the millennium.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Most regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were easier in early Asian trade on Tuesday as the dollar managed to erase earlier losses against the yen on buying by Japanese investors and importers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders in Tokyo said the dollar was also supported by wariness over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of Japan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Newsroom +852 2843-6960; Fax +852 2845-0636 hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9700zq4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
