\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Up; \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Pushes NT$ Higher \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 1999\par 10:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took advantage of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight sell-off in the major \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily during Asian trading Tuesday to drive the New Taiwan dollar back up. \par \par \uc2  Other Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also benefited from the U.S. dollar's weakness against the yen, with the Singapore dollar and baht both rising during Asian trading. \par \par \uc2  The Korean won, however, was pushed down steeply to hit its lowest level in two months as heavy government-directed dollar buying by state-owned banks caught the market short of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Once again, however, attention was focused on the New Taiwan dollar market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of China - the Taiwanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - took the opportunity afforded by the U.S. dollar's weakness against the yen to push the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to levels it last saw a week ago, when relations between Taiwan and China turned sour. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very serious about limiting the impact of the crisis on the exchange rate," said the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at one major foreign bank in Taipei, estimating that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounted for over a third of Tuesday's onshore market volume of US$530.50 million. \par \par \uc2  The coming days will see the authorities continuing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the exchange rate stable, or even to drive the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower should the dollar lose more ground against the yen, said the trading chief. \par \par \uc2  At the close of onshore dealing Tuesday, the U.S. dollar was quoted at NT$32.257, down from NT$32.332 the previous day. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 20-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0830GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7k05baj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
