\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar revives in Asia after overnight mugging. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 730 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 1999\par 07:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 20 (Reuters) - The dollar was looking a bit healthier by midday in Asia after an overnight shakeout which led traders to speculate on possible European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and surprised them by the Bank of Japan's absence. \par \par \uc2  It perked up as short-term players booked profit on the yen's overnight surge to five-week highs, with traders in Asia still wary of the BOJ despite a Japanese holiday. \par \par \uc2  But most analysts dismissed the likelihood of the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in thin Singapore and \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "To be sure during a Tokyo holiday you could have a big impact because the market's thinner. But are you influencing the people who are going to be moving the market?" said Andrew Dermot-Fung, treasury economist at Standard Chartered. \par \par \uc2  "The answer has to be no... The big risk is if they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  during a Tokyo holiday, then London comes in and says, 'Thankyou very much,' and we're back to where we were," he said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 118.57/60 yen at 0455 GMT against its New York close at 118.15/25 yen. The euro was at $1.0294/04 against $1.0307/12. Euro/yen was at 122.21/3.21 against 121.73. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said the BOJ could also be signalling tolerance of a wider trading range for dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2  "Overall I think they are happy in a range of 115-125 and I think they have to be more flexible. To defend the 120 yen level in a stubborn way is difficult against the market," said Karl Broecker, head of treasury at Landesbank Baden-Wuerttemberg. \par \par \uc2  Broecker told Reuters Television the BOJ was likely to step in and check prices if the dollar fell below 117.50 yen, but added that this was likely to be aimed at stabilising the market. \par \par \uc2  Further gains in the dollar were, however, blocked by offers left by Japanese exporters and investors below 119 yen. \par \par \uc2  Analysts noted that the euro's overnight bounce had also removed pressure on the euro/yen exchange rate - a major source of concern for Japanese officials. \par \par \uc2  "Japanese exporters need to sell euro/yen more than they need to sell dollar/yen. They went into European assets at the end of last year and that really hasn't paid off," said a senior trader at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly to block the yen's rise against the dollar and euro in the past month, with much official fretting that a strong yen could smother Japan's infant recovery. \par \par \uc2  The euro won a reprieve overnight amid speculation the ECB had stepped in to stem the seven-month-old unit's embarrassing slide towards parity with the dollar. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk was fuelled by ECB Vice President Christian Noyer's comment on Monday that the euro is now being watched much more closely than before. \par \par \uc2  No official confirmation was available and there was also talk of large hedge fund orders in a market severely short of euros, but analysts said covert \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action could not be ruled out. \par \par \uc2  "The action, if it was taken, was in a very sensitive way. Simply an open \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have failed and this would be a blow in the face of the ECB. But getting the market wrong-footed helped to engineer this recovery (in the euro)," said Broecker. \par \par \uc2  He noted that expectations of a strong German Ifo business climate index for June should also give a boost to the euro. Analysts in a Reuters poll predicted a rise in the headline western Germany index to 91.1 from 90.4 in May. \par \par \uc2  But few were willing to bet on the euro's rebound being more than a mild respite and dealers said its near-term prospects remained shaky. \par \par \uc2  "The economists are saying the ECB could hike rates soon, European growth could pick up soon, but soon is not something we trade on," said one. \par \par \uc2  Thio Chin Loo, strategist at Paribas, agreed that it was too early to call a reversal in the euro's overall downtrend. \par \par \uc2  "I wouldn't be convinced that the euro has turned around until it closes above $1.05," she said. \par \par \uc2  ((Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk (65) 870-3090;fax (65) 870-3787; email: asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7k042av\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
