\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 :  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Supports New Taiwan Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 1999\par 10:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  supported the New Taiwan dollar during Asian trading Monday, but \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  elsewhere in Asia weakened as the heightened tensions between Taiwan and China continued to erode confidence in regional markets. \par \par \uc2  Once again the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of China - Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling U.S. dollars to arrest the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall. Dealers estimate that the Taiwanese authorities have now spent over $1 billion supporting the New Taiwan dollar since the cross-straits crisis over Taiwan's status erupted a week ago. \par \par \uc2  But with $97.70 billion in foreign reserves at the end of June, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not about to permit any significant fall in the value of the New Taiwan dollar, agreed traders and analysts. \par \par \uc2  By the end of local trading Monday, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had pushed the U.S. dollar down to NT$32.332 from NT$32.361 at Saturday's close, and well below the five-week high of NT$32.425 the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit in Friday's intraday trade. \par \par \uc2  In the offshore market, the premium on non-deliverable U.S. dollar/New Taiwan dollar forwards (NDF) subsided from the highs seen on Friday as buying pressure abated. \par \par \uc2  With many market participants having successfully covered their exposure to the Taiwanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in frenzied dealing last week, much of Monday's activity was generated by traders managing their positions. \par \par \uc2  "Volumes have eased off," said one Singapore-based broker. "But this is a hairy market, which could still move very rapidly." \par \par \uc2  Late Monday, brokers were quoting the one-month NDF at a premium over the spot rate of 40/60 points, well down from levels of 230/280 points seen late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The 12-month rate was at 370/410, down from 630/680 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 19-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0851GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7j05bsl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
