\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Dn Midday On Lower Short-Term Rates; 1-Yr Fwd Up \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 1999\par 05:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is weaker against the U.S. dollar midday Friday as it continues to fall in reaction to lower short-term interbank interest rates. \par \par \uc2  At 0216 GMT (10:16 p.m. Thursday EDT), it was trading at HK$7.7597 to the U.S. dollar, weaker than HK$7.7594 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The market has now got a reason to buy (U.S. dollars)," a dealer at a local bank said. Hong Kong interbank offered rates dropped Thursday after the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave a sharp boost to liquidity as part of its normal \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight rate fell to about 1.5% late Thursday on the move, although rates further out the yield curve didn't fall as much. It has since climbed back to about 4.87%, and is expected to hover around that level for the rest of the session, barring further action from the HKMA. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, premiums have popped back up a bit on profit-taking, the trader said. The one-year premium was trading around 840 points over the spot rate, after hitting 790 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "We've seen the low for the time being," another dealer said. Forward premiums tend to fall with short-term interest rates to reflect a narrowing of the spread over U.S. rates. But he said the market would have to see interbank rates a little lower and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar weaken to the HKMA's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level of HK$7.76 this session before the one-year forward tests the 800 level again. \par \par \uc2  -By Dow Jones Newswires; (852)2802-7002 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0309GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv79055qq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
