\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Open Dn;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  By MAS Suspected \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 1999\par 03:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have opened down against the U.S. dollar early Wednesday, following what brokers believe to have been overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Heavy buying in London hours propelled the U.S. dollar up sharply from a low of S$1.6880, triggering stop-loss buy orders and driving the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as high as S$1.7005 overnight. \par \par \uc2  "This looks like \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to me," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  broker in Singapore. "All the dollar shorts have been squeezed out." \par \par \uc2  At 0045 GMT (8:45 p.m. EDT) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.6955, off its overnight high, but still well above S$1.6890 late in Asia Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the Thai baht (THB), the U.S. dollar is quoted at THB36.8600, up from THB38.7800 late the day before in sympathy with its rise against the Singapore dollar. Most dealers see the market maintaining its recent THB36.7500 to THB36.9000 through the coming session, however. \par \par \uc2  Against the Indonesian rupiah (IDR), the U.S. dollar is at IDR6,730 compared with IDR6,712 late the day before. \par \par \uc2  Against the South Korean won (KRW), the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has opened at KRW1,169.20, up a fraction from KRW1,169.00 at the previous close. \par \par \uc2  Trading in the Philippine peso (PHP) and the new Taiwan dollar has yet to begin. At Tuesday's close the U.S. dollar was at PHP38.110 and NT$32.282. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 07-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0100GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv77053of\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
