\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Unmoved By BOJ; Philippine Peso Drops \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 1999\par 10:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen barely caused a stir in Asia's regional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Monday, as most other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked sideways or trended only moderately lower. \par \par \uc2  The sole exception was the Philippine peso, which sank back as market players trimmed their long positions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in response to the peso's shrinking yield spread over the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the Philippines' benchmark treasury bill dropped Monday to its lowest level in over 12 years, falling to 8.474%, down steeply from 13.459% at the beginning of the year. \par \par \uc2  "Clearly the interest rate differential is going against the peso, with local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rates coming down, and U.S. dollar rates having been tightened," said David Simmonds, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Although the factors driving peso yields lower - a declining inflation rate and buoyant exports - should be positive for the peso in the long run, in the short term the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be set for further weakness as traders cut back long peso carry trades. \par \par \uc2  "The market appears uncomfortable over whether the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy to pursue a stable exchange rate can coexist alongside its aggressive easy monetary stance, especially after the U.S. hiked rates by 25 basis points," wrote analysts at Standard Chartered Bank in a research note dated Monday. \par \par \uc2  By the end of local trading Monday, short covering had pushed the U.S. dollar up to finish the day at PHP38.145, up from PHP38.073 at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 05-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0830GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7504zzp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
