\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Weaker Amid Quarterly Selling; Mkt Eyes Fed \b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 1999\par 05:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is weaker midmorning Wednesday, drifting in a narrow range amid thin dealing as foreign players repatriate funds at the quarter end. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar was trading at HK$7.7585 per U.S. dollar at 0255 GMT (10:55 p.m. Tuesday EDT), down from HK$7.7581 late Tuesday. It reached HK$7.7587 before settling back. \par \par \uc2  "There's typical seasonal demand (for U.S. dollars); it's mostly just repatriation by foreign entities," said a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  player. \par \par \uc2  He also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is likely to slide further toward its pegged \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level of HK$7.7591 "in tandem with the (\b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's) gradual plan for letting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slide." Hong Kong's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seeks to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  one pip per day until the U.S. dollar reaches the official peg rate of HK$7.7800. Thin trading toward the end of the session may accentuate the move. \par \par \uc2  Otherwise, traders said dealings are calm as the market awaits the outcome from the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy meeting later Wednesday. U.S. central bankers are expected to boost interest rates a quarter-percentage point, a move widely priced into the market and expected to have little effect here. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers have been selling longer-term forwards in anticipation of a narrower gap between U.S. and Hong Kong interest rates, and a consequently weaker Hong Kong dollar. The one-year premium is 810 points over the spot exchange rate, compared with about 830 points late Tuesday. Some traders say it could go as low as 750 points in the wake of the Fed meeting. \par \par \uc2  Local markets will be closed Thursday to mark the second anniversary of Hong Kong's reversion to China. \par \par \uc2  -by Dow Jones Newswires; (852)2802-7002 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 30-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0342GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6u04wov\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
