\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Steady Midday; Focus Shifts To Forwards Market \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 1999\par 05:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is steady and stuck in a range-bound trading Friday morning, with activity focused on the forwards market. \par \par \uc2  "There's a bit of buying in the forwards market," said one dealer, explaining that players are hedging against an expected weakening of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the weeks ahead. \par \par \uc2  The one-year forward rate nudged up to about 890 points over the spot rate, from 880 late Thursday. It's been moving up since midweek as the Hong Kong dollar weakened in response to lower short-term interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar is trading at HK$7.7581 per U.S. dollar at 0229 GMT (10:29 p.m. EDT), little changed from its level late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Players also await the meeting Tuesday and Wednesday of the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee and "people are a bit worried about a rise in U.S. rates," said a dealer with a U.S. bank. Many traders say a hike of a quarter-percentage point is priced in, but some are concerned that the Fed might raise rates by as much as a half-percentage point to stave off any future inflationary pressures. \par \par \uc2  Otherwise, another dealer with a U.K. firm said it's very unlikely the Hong Kong dollar will break out of range for the next few days. Because short-term interest rates here are higher than U.S. rates, there's ample support around HK$7.7580, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate at HK$7.7586 damps selling pressure on the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -by Dow Jones Newswires; (852)2802-7002 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 25-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0340GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6p04twh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
