\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regional firmer, rupiah bucks trend. \b0\par\par\uc2 830 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 1999\par 11:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0900 GMT - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended a quiet day slightly \par \par \uc2  firmer as money continues to flow into regional financial \par \par \uc2  markets to profit from the preceived economic recovery. \par \par \uc2      But trading ranges were narrow as dealers feared more \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not only by the BOJ but by some of the regional \par \par \uc2  central banks as well, particularly in South Korea. \par \par \uc2      **** The yen firmed slightly, shrugging off Sakakibara's \par \par \uc2  comments that he was watching movements in dollar/yen and \par \par \uc2  euro/yen very carefully. \par \par \uc2      Traders said the dollar was likely to remain under pressure \par \par \uc2  in the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as hopes run high \par \par \uc2  over a Japanese economic recovery. \par \par \uc2      *** The Korean won firmed after some good news from rating \par \par \uc2  agency Fitch IBCA. \par \par \uc2      Fitch upgraded South Korea's long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  rating to BBB from BBB-, citing the strong reassertion of the \par \par \uc2  country's traditional economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2      The international credit rating agency said in a statement \par \par \uc2  it had also raised the country's short-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  rating to F2 from F3, in recognition of the continued build-up \par \par \uc2  of external liquidity, which has exceeded earlier expectations. \par \par \uc2  A Fitch official told Reuters Television that any future \par \par \uc2  upgrade would depend on what happens in the corporate and \par \par \uc2  banking sectors. \par \par \uc2  *** IMF Asia Pacific director Hubert Neiss, speaking at a \par \par \uc2  debt conference in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said he believed South Korea's \par \par \uc2  recent direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was \par \par \uc2  aimed at smoothing moves in the won. \par \par \uc2  *** The Thai baht was steady with the authorities attacking \par \par \uc2  rating agency Moody's for their report which said Thai banks \par \par \uc2  remained heavily insolvent. \par \par \uc2  Kiatchai Sopasathienpong, director of the Bank of \par \par \uc2  Thailand's financial institutions supervision department, said \par \par \uc2  Moody's negative views on Thai banks were not shared by other \par \par \uc2  ratings agencies, such as Standard & Poor's and Fitch IBCA. \par \par \uc2      "Moody's holds rather negative views of us and they have an \par \par \uc2  impact...the stock market was disappointed that it did not \par \par \uc2  upgrade Thai banks...," he said. \par \par \uc2      Moody's said all Thai banks remained "heavily insolvent in \par \par \uc2  true economic terms" though with varying outlooks. It said \par \par \uc2  despite the banking sector's deep capital impairment, \par \par \uc2  regulatory forbearance was substantial. \par \par \uc2  *** Thailand's Prime Minister Chuan Leekpai reaffirmed \par \par \uc2  official estimates of 1.0 percent GDP growth for 1999 and 3.0 \par \par \uc2  percent for 2000. \par \par \uc2  Chuan said that the economy had shown clearer signs of \par \par \uc2  recovery following the stabilisation of the baht, a period of \par \par \uc2  low inflation and falling interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The prime minister also said inflation for 2000 was \par \par \uc2  estimated at 3.0 percent against a projected 0.5 percent for \par \par \uc2  1999. \par \par \uc2  *** Malaysian news agency Bernama quoted First Deputy \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Wong See Wah as saying that the finance \par \par \uc2  ministry is looking at revising its official GDP growth \par \par \uc2  forecast of one percent for 1999. \par \par \uc2  Malaysia on Wednesday announced its GDP estimates, which \par \par \uc2  showed a 1.3 percent contraction in the first quarter of 1999 \par \par \uc2  year on-year, less than the 1.6 percent recently indicated by \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the economy had begun to rebound in \par \par \uc2  the past three months, and GDP would strengthen in the second \par \par \uc2  half of the year. \par \par \uc2  *** The rupiah bucked the regional trend giving up some of \par \par \uc2  its recent strong gains but the profit-taking came as no \par \par \uc2  surprise. \par \par \uc2  IMF Asia Pacific director Hubert Neiss said there was still \par \par \uc2  room for the rupiah to strengthen, which would be good for \par \par \uc2  confidence in Asia. \par \par \uc2  *** Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Syahril Sabirin told \par \par \uc2  reporters he expected month-on-month inflation in June to be \par \par \uc2  zero or negative, versus May inflation of minus 0.2 percent. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Economics minister Ginandjar Kartasasmita said \par \par \uc2  the government had not yet changed the assumed average exchange \par \par \uc2  rate for the rupiah in the state budget despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \par \par \uc2  rise. \par \par \uc2      *** Hong Kong's April retail sales fell 10 percent in value \par \par \uc2  year-on-year but rose one percent from March. \par \par \uc2      Total retail sales was a provisional HK$14.3 billion in \par \par \uc2  April. \par \par \uc2   Change o