\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Flat Midday; Strong Hibor Slows Weakening Trend \b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1999\par 05:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is steady Tuesday morning, with high interbank rates continuing to slow what has been a weakening trend in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  At 0245 GMT (10:45 p.m. EDT Monday), the local dollar was flat at HK$7.7579 per U.S. dollar compared with late Monday. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a European bank said that if short-term interbank interest rates weren't close to or slightly above 6%, they'd expect the Hong Kong dollar to be hovering near the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's HK$7.7583 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. \par \par \uc2  That rate is intentionally being brought down by one "pip" (0.0001 point) per day until it reaches the peg rate of HK$7.80 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  However, liquidity in money markets is tight, and there's no sign the overnight and one-week rate will drop below 6% anytime soon. \par \par \uc2  Traders at two European banks said if those rates hold close to where they are or rise Tuesday morning, there's a good possibility the HKMA will try to ease the tight liquidity by lending short-term money in afternoon trading. It was believed to have done so early Monday, when short-term rates opened at over 6%. \par \par \uc2  Many of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's larger players are trading cautiously. While the differential between Hong Kong dollar and U.S. dollar rates make it attractive to hold the local dollar, they're aware that rates aren't likely to go much higher and that the HKMA could be ready to push those rates down. \par \par \uc2  The local dollar is expected to trade in a narrow HK7.7577-HK7.7579 range against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Forward market activity remains slow. Investors who had hedged Hong Kong dollar positions last week on concerns about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakening closed their positions early Monday. The six-month premium of 280 points is nearly flat from late Monday's 275 points over the spot rate. The one-year premium is 960 points, compared with 950 points. \par \par \uc2  -By Adam Najberg; (852)2802-7002; naj@asiaonline.net \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0330GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6m04ra5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
