\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 : Rupiah Shrugs Of BOJ To Hit 8-Mo High \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 1999\par 10:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--Rupiah bulls ignored repeated dollar-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan to bid up the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to its highest level in eight months during Asian trading hours Monday. \par \par \uc2  Other Asian markets failed to shrug off the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the region finished the day lower, dragged down by the BOJ's yen sales. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment toward Indonesian markets remained buoyant, despite a further delay to the already protracted vote count following the country's parliamentary election two weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's electoral commission admitted Monday that it will be unable to produce a final poll result until July 8, but the news did little to deter foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  "There is a lot of money going into the Indonesian stock market, so people are buying rupiah to buy equities," said the rupiah trader at one U.S. bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  He estimated that overseas investors had bought as much as $200 million-worth of rupiah by early Monday afternoon, encouraged by a 1% rise in the local stock index and the announcement that Bank Internasional Indonesia is planning a private stock placement to assist its recapitalization. \par \par \uc2  Dealers also cited weekend comments from Stanley Fischer, first deputy managing director at the International Monetary Fund, as a strong reason to buy the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Addressing a press conference in Jakarta, Fisher said that the rupiah still has further room to appreciate. He even raised the possibility that the rupiah may get so strong that Bank Indonesia might buy dollars to hold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down. \par \par \uc2  "These comments are very, very positive for the rupiah," said a trader at a second U.S. bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Fischer's remarks lent weight to last week's comments from Indonesia's senior economics minister, Ginandjar Kartasasmita, and Bank Indonesia's governor, Sjahril Sabirin, both of whom said the dollar would at fair value between IDR6,500 and IDR7,000. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 21-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0830GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6l04ok6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
