\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Stronger Due To High Short-Term Interbank Rates \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 1999\par 05:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--High short-term interbank interest rates sparked an early move into the Hong Kong dollar Monday, strengthening the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  There was early buying by Singapore-based banks, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar is trading at HK$7.7577 at 0330 GMT (11:30 p.m. EDT), after hitting its strongest intraday level of HK$7.7575 very early in the session. \par \par \uc2  While the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is nearly flat from late Friday's levels, it had been expected to continue a weakening trend of the past few weeks, which has seen it bump against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. \par \par \uc2  That rate has been weakening by one "pip" (0.0001 point) per day since April 1 and will continue to move until it reaches the official peg rate of HK$7.80 per US$1.00. \par \par \uc2  The treasury chief at a domestic bank said that with the overnight and one-week interbank rates at over 6% early, investors took on short-term Hong Kong dollar positions, avoiding what many had expected to be a day when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakens to HK$7.7580. \par \par \uc2  The quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen lending in short-term money markets early Monday, taking those rates below 6%. \par \par \uc2  With the move into the local dollar, some investors squared long-term forward hedging positions. The six-month premium is down to 295 points over the spot rate from 320 points late Friday. The one-year premium is 1000 points, down from 1050. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they're seeing some hedging in short-term forward markets, likely due to the early spot activity. But premiums haven't risen significantly. \par \par \uc2  Some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors are displaying jitters over tight liquidity in the interbank system, with a continued forecast of a negative balance in the aggregate balance of clearing accounts banks maintain with the HKMA. Until there are signs of more liquidity, they're expected to be cautious, the treasury chief said. \par \par \uc2  -By Adam S. Najberg; (852)2802-7002; naj@asiaonline.net \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0354GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6l04nlm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
