\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Weaker;Holds Near  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Rate Before Holiday \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1999\par 05:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--Trading in the spot Hong Kong dollar has quieted midday Thursday ahead of a three-day weekend, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  still holding close to the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trading at HK$7.7577 per U.S. dollar at 0330 GMT (11:30 p.m. EDT Wednesday), just a touch weaker than late Wednesday's HK$7.7575 and right below the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's HK$7.7578 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a U.S. bank said no one is willing to challenge the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate and trading has thus far been limited to small, two-way activity, leaving the local dollar in a HK$7.7575-77 range. He said he expects the Hong Kong dollar to remain in that range before markets close for the Dragon Boat holiday Friday. \par \par \uc2  With the spot quiet and because U.S. inflation data Wednesday was benign, concerns of an imminent interest rate hike have eased, Hong Kong dollar hedging has slowed in the forward markets. \par \par \uc2  Some investors have closed out small positions and taken their profits, and most of the market's usual big players aren't active so far Thursday. The one-year forward is quoted at 1,000 points over the spot rate, down from 1,050 points late Wednesday. The six-month premium is 310 points, down from 315 points. \par \par \uc2  The local rate-setting cartel won't meet Friday because of the holiday. It's next policy meeting will be next week, and if U.S. data continue to dispel concerns of a rate hike there, local dealers said they don't expect pressure on the Hong Kong Association of Banks to raise Hong Kong's deposit rates. \par \par \uc2  -By Adam S. Najberg; (852)2802-7002; naj@asiaonline.net \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0342GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6h04oia\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
