\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Dn Late; Fwds Inch Up In Muted Reaction To Korea \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1999\par 11:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is a touch weaker late Tuesday in the wake of soft interbank rates, while forward premiums inched higher in afternoon dealings amid North-South Korea tensions. \par \par \uc2  At 0900 GMT (5:00 a.m. EDT), the spot Hong Kong dollar was quoted at HK$7.7575 per U.S. dollar, down from late Monday's HK$7.7570. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar touched the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate of HK$7.7576 in late afternoon trade. \par \par \uc2  The overnight interbank rate is at 4%, after dipping down to 3% intraday on aggressive lending by a major U.K. lender. \par \par \uc2  Traders said it wasn't clear why the U.K. bank was intent on pushing the rates lower, which was encouraging switching into U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  One trader with a European bank noted there are many bids sitting behind the HK$7.7576 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. As a result, the spot rate will likely stay close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, he said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, gunfire exchanged between North and South Korean gunboats earlier Tuesday helped push up forwards slightly in early afternoon trade. \par \par \uc2  But by late in the day, concerns were easing on the view that the tensions weren't likely to escalate. \par \par \uc2  The one-year forward premium is quoted late at 1,040 points, compared to 1,030 points midday Tuesday, but still lower than 1,080 points late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The six-month premium is quoted at 305 points from 300 points midday, but down from 320 points late in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market remains on hold until Wednesday's release of U.S. inflation data, which is expected to provide clues on whether the U.S. Federal Reserve will raise its rates at its policy meeting June 29-30. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong tends to adjust rates in line with the U.S. due to its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 15-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0936GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6f04i2w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
