\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Flat Late Despite Drop In Overnight Rate \b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 10:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar was flat late Monday in thin dealings as stubbornly firm longer-term interbank rates are supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite a sharp drop in the volatile overnight rate. \par \par \uc2  Around 0800 GMT (4:00 a.m. EDT), the local unit was trading at HK$7.7570 to the U.S. dollar, flat from its late Friday level. \par \par \uc2  That steady position comes despite a steep fall in the overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate to 1.00% from 5.75% late last week. \par \par \uc2  A trader at a local bank said that all other interbank rates remain near their levels last week, with the three-month benchmark rate at 5.75%, up from 5.50%. \par \par \uc2  Traders report little activity in the spot market for Hong Kong dollars as many participants sit on the sidelines to await an expected interest rate hike in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Many traders expect the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee to raise rates by a quarter-percentage point at its next meeting on June 29-30. \par \par \uc2  However, the interest rate jitters, compounded by a rise in the 30-year U.S. Treasury yield to over 6% Friday, is leading to a rise in Hong Kong dollar forward premiums, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Interest rates in Hong Kong tend to track those in the U.S. due to the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The one-year premium was quoted at 1,080 points over the spot rate late Monday, up from 1,000 points late in the previous session. The six-month premium was 320 points, up from 300 points. \par \par \uc2  The local bank trader said he expects the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar rate to hover just under the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate as interest rate concerns continue to dog the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the rate at which the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pledged to covert local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for U.S. dollars stood at HK$7.7575. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0834GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6e04ixo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
