\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 : BOJ Spoils Party For Regional Bulls \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 10:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--Massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan to push the yen lower spoilt what would otherwise have been a field day for Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bulls Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah, the Singapore dollar, the Philippine peso and the new Taiwan dollar still managed to end Asian hours higher on the day, despite the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action. But the South Korean won and the Thai baht both closed lower in parallel with the yen. \par \par \uc2  Monday's trading started on a strongly positive note for regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The admission over the weekend by Indonesia's governing Golkar party that it had lost last week's parliamentary elections, boosted the rupiah (IDR) to its highest level in six months. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's climb, which saw the U.S. dollar fall to IDR7,525 in early dealing, boosted the Singapore dollar too. \par \par \uc2  As the U.S. dollar came under pressure against the yen, falling to a low of Y117.91 in early trading, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also sold down against the Singapore dollar. As successive stop-loss sales orders were triggered in thin market conditions, the U.S. dollar dropped to a one-month low of S$1.7040, according to brokers on the island republic. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar's fall against the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was soon arrested, however, as the Bank of Japan's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompted market players to cover their short positions in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 14-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0830GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6e04ix0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
