\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends steady on export hopes. \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 06:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 14 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed steady on Monday, continuing to stay at high levels, on expectations that China's exports would show a recovery in May, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished at an intraday high of 8.2775, unchanged from Friday. \par \par \uc2  After the market closed on Monday, customs said that exports rose 4.2 percent year-on-year in May to $15.53 billion. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said May's year-on-year rise in exports was the first rise this year and further improvement was expected in exports in the coming months. \par \par \uc2  "Traders expects more \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to flow into the market in the near term," said a dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  "This convinced some traders to build yuan positions, helping the yuan to stay at high levels." \par \par \uc2  The yuan now stands near a historical closing high of 8.2773, which was reached on December 8 last year. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan could undergo a correction in the next few days, but improving exports could help it resume an upturn to test the record closing high in the short term. \par \par \uc2  There were no signs that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the tightly-controlled market on Monday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan touched an intraday low of 8.2778 with most business done at 8.2776, they said. The weighted average price on Friday was 8.2777. \par \par \uc2  The local unit closed higher against the Japanese yen at 6.8988 to 100 yen from Friday's 6.9650. The yuan's rise followed a fall in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the international market as the Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished easier against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar at 1.0680 to HK$1 against 1.0670. \par \par \uc2     ((Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  reutersh@uninet.com.cn)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6e06knt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
