\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Slightly Weaker Midday; Near  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Level \b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 1999\par 05:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is slightly weaker against the U.S. dollar midday Tuesday, hovering near a key \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level, but market participants say the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain stuck in its current tight trading band for the time being. \par \par \uc2  Sustained, but moderate, selling of the Hong Kong dollar for U.S. dollars over the past few sessions is keeping the local unit within a few pips of Tuesday's HK$7.7569 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. But stability reigns in local money markets, and traders are ruling out any breach of the rate at which the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pledged to step into the market to support its local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 0300 GMT (11:00 p.m. Monday EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7568 to the U.S. dollar, slightly weaker than the HK$7.7564 seen late Monday. \par \par \uc2  A total of HK$566 million will leave Hong Kong's banking system Tuesday, having been sold for U.S. dollars Friday. A further HK$543 million will depart Thursday, as a result of transactions conducted early Tuesday under Hong Kong's T+2 settlement system. \par \par \uc2  But the selling has had little impact on local interbank rates, which automatically rise on any substantial outflow of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because of the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -board system. The volatile overnight Hong Kong interbank offered rate is quoted 4.75% midday Tuesday, up from 4.375% late Monday. \par \par \uc2  And the forward market is also decidedly calm Tuesday, with longer-term premiums declining, indicating increased confidence in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the view that interest rates might not be moving higher. The one-year premium is quoted at 950 points midday Tuesday, down from 975 points late Monday, on what a trader at a local bank said was some houses unwinding long U.S. dollar positions. The six-month premium is quoted at 250 points, down from 275 points. \par \par \uc2  That's putting traders at ease over the outflows, with most expecting the Hong Kong dollar to remain in its current range just below the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, barring any major additional selling of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0322GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6804ay8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
