\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Hong Kong - June 8. \b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 1999\par 03:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, June 8 (Reuters) - These are some of the leading stories in Hong Kong newspapers on Tuesday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy. \par \par \uc2  SING TAO DAILY - The Hong Kong government will extend the freeze on public fees and charges it imposed during the Asian financial crisis for six months due to public pressure, say sources. \par \par \uc2  - The Health Department has banned the sale of meat and dairy products, including 35 baby formula products, from four major European countries. These products are believed to have been possibly contaminated with dioxin. \par \par \uc2  MING PAO DAILY NEWS - The Executive Council will approve the construction of a new suspension bridge to link Hong Kong with Shenzhen West across the border. This is a joint project of the two governments and the completion date is set for 2005. \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG ECONOMIC TIMES - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chief Executive Joseph Yam has indicated that Hong Kong will have to follow the U.S. if it increases its interest rates in the long run. \par \par \uc2  - (Editorial) The competition among Internet services providers has a great social impact as Internet subscribers in Hong Kong may exceed the two-million mark in two years. \par \par \uc2  APPLE DAILY - Hong Kong's economy suffered an estimated loss of HK$1.7 billion in half a day on Monday, due to typhoon Maggie. \par \par \uc2  - Competition for mortgage business among local banks is reaching a cut-throat phase as Kwong On Bank reduced the rate offered to 6.88 percent for the first year. \par \par \uc2  SOUTH CHINA MORNING POST - Conglomerate Wheelock's planned privatisation of upmarket retailer Lane Crawford International faces collapse after a group of minority investors pledged to vote against the proposal. \par \par \uc2  - The government should relax its traditional laissez-faire policy and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to oversee \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's transformation into a cyber-economy. according to newly released research from the Bank of East Asia. \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG STANDARD - Cheung Kong (Holdings) controversial proposal to develop a cruise liner terminal in North Point has attracted 17 objections, raising the prospect of a delay in its implementation or even the possibility that it may be scrapped. \par \par \uc2  - Hong Kong has slipped to fifth place in the ranking of countries holding the world's largest \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. The reserves have declined by US$600 million to US$88.9 billion at the end of last month from the end-April level of US$89.5 billion. \par \par \uc2  WEN WEI PO - Complaints against property sale agents are expected to increase this year. Forty percent of complaints involved sales commission. \par \par \uc2  ((Hong Kong Newsroom +852 2843 6441, Fax +852 2845 0636 hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6806zkr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
