\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Near  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Rate Midday On Funds Outflow \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 1999\par 05:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is slightly weaker midday Friday, hovering near a key \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level, as the market reacts to an expected outflow of funds from the banking system. \par \par \uc2  Around 0300 GMT (11:00 p.m. Thursday EDT), the local unit is quoted at HK$7.7564 to the U.S. dollar, slightly weaker than the HK$7.7561 seen late Thursday, but still very near Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level of HK$7.7565. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market was eyeing a moderate-sized sale of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for U.S. dollars conducted late Thursday in overseas markets that will drain HK$271 million from the banking system on Monday, under Hong Kong's T+2 settlement system. \par \par \uc2  But traders also said the transaction appears to be commercial - and not speculative - in nature. \par \par \uc2  "If it was speculation, there shouldn't be this kind of amount, it should be HK$500 million or HK$1 billion and there should be continuous buying (of U.S. dollars) in the TT (spot market)," said a trader at a U.S. bank in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  The trader added that he doesn't expect a test Friday of the rate at which the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it will step into the market to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the forwards market, premiums opened slightly higher Friday as Hong Kong traders got their first chance to react to the funds outflow. But premiums have since eased from their morning highs, with the one-year premium quoted at 1000 points midday, down from 1070 points late Thursday. The six-month premium is 305 points, down from 315 points. \par \par \uc2  The market has for the most part recovered from rumors Thursday that China was about to devalue the yuan, traders said. The rumors, which were quickly quashed by Chinese authorities, stemmed from a misinterpretation of a tightening of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls announced Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Midday Thursday, the volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 4.75%, up from 1.5% late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 04-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0338GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6404a6f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
