\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Steady Midday; Fwd Premiums Fall On Pft-Taking \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 1999\par 05:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong dollar forward premiums are lower early Tuesday from overnight levels in New York and London, with investors taking profits as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  steadies. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar was nearly flat at HK$7.7545 at 0235 GMT (10:35 p.m. Monday EDT) from HK$7.7546 per U.S. dollar late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Worries about Argentina abandoning its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board caused the spot exchange rate to weaken and forward premiums to rise for most of Monday in Asia, on nervous hedging and speculation that the local dollar would weaken further over the next year. \par \par \uc2  Those concerns started to fade toward the end of Asian trading Monday, but nervous investors in London and New York, their jitters fueled by hedge funds rolling over short forward positions, took forward premiums back close to intraday highs. \par \par \uc2  The one-year premium, which peaked at 1080 points over the spot rate early Monday, had eased to 975 points by the end of the Asian trading day. Overnight, that rate climbed back to 1020 points and opened there in Hong Kong Tuesday. It's now quoted at 990 as hedge funds and other investors take advantage of the volatility and take profits. \par \par \uc2  The six-month premium has also been volatile, but has returned to 285 points, just above late Asia's 280-point level. \par \par \uc2  The head of money markets at a U.S. bank said the Hong Kong dollar should hold steady and stay well below the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate of HK$7.7555 because of the overnight fall in the Dow Jones Industrial Average. \par \par \uc2  The money markets chief said the fall in the U.S. stock index has lessened concerns in Hong Kong of an imminent rise in U.S. interest rates. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 25-05-99 \par \par \uc2  0323GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv5p03woy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
