\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Strengthens Early; Cash Inflows Return To Stk Mkt \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 1999\par 04:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is stronger early Tuesday in thin trade, helped by cash inflows to the territory's stock market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0205 GMT (10:05 p.m. EDT Monday), the Hong Kong dollar was quoted at HK$7.7506 against the U.S. dollar, compared with HK$7.7512 late Monday. The local unit has traded between HK$7.7504 and HK$7.7508 so far Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they suspect the renewal of "hot money" into the territory has helped the local unit, although its gain is distorted by the thin market. \par \par \uc2  "There's probably capital inflows," said an Australian bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  At 0221 GMT (10:21 p.m. EDT Monday), the blue-chip Hang Seng Index is up 215.02 points, or 1.6%, to 13,552.09, after rising as high as 2.6% immediately after the open. \par \par \uc2  Dealers also noted that market holidays in both Tokyo and London are keeping a lid on business locally, noting that the Hong Kong dollar often comes under selling pressure when trading starts in London and closes in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  The interbank market is steady, with the volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate quoted at 4.50%, unchanged from late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums continue to fall, reflecting overall confidence in the Hong Kong dollar, which is now trading 28 points away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level, its broadest spread in seven trading sessions. \par \par \uc2  In the forward market, the one-month premium is quoted at an eight-point discount to the spot Hong Kong dollar, compared with a six-point discount late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The three-month premium is quoted at 21 points, down from 30 points previously. The six-month premium is quoted at 150 points, down from 175. The one-year premium is quoted at 690 points, down from 750. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2832 2336; sean.kennedy@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 04-05-99 \par \par \uc2  0243GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv5403cwa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
