\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Weaker Late; Adrift In Thin Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 1999\par 09:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is slightly weaker late Monday after modest sales of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened a thin market in which volume had virtually evaporated due to a market holiday in Japan. \par \par \uc2  Around 0700 GMT (3:00 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7512 against the U.S. dollar, compared with HK$7.7508 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The local unit has traded in a narrow range between HK$7.7509 and HK$7.7512 so far Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there's nothing to focus on, and the Hong Kong dollar is just drifting. "There's nothing new out there. It's very quiet. There's nothing to drive the market," said an Australian bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rates is quoted at 4.50%, down from 5.00% late Friday. \par \par \uc2  A local bank treasurer said the holiday in Japan, and another holiday in London, has sidelined many players for the moment. \par \par \uc2  Despite the slight weakening in the spot Hong Kong dollar, forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums - a bellwether of confidence in the local unit - are generally lower, indicating that no one is too concerned about the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar is still 21 basis points away from the HK$7.7533 level which would trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the territory's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level has been moving by one basis point a day since April 1, in a phased devaluation announced by the HKMA last September. \par \par \uc2  In the forwards market, the one-month is quoted at a six-point discount to the spot Hong Kong dollar, compared with a two-point discount late Friday. The three-month premium is quoted at 30 points, down from 35 points. The six-month premium is at 175 points, unchanged from 175 previously. The one-year premium is quoted at 750 points, down from 770 previously. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2832 2336; sean.kennedy@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 03-05-99 \par \par \uc2  0728GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv5303ax3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
