\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Weaker Late; Pushes Through HK$7.7500 Level \b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 1999\par 09:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is weaker against the U.S. dollar late Friday, mauled by low short-term rates, which have triggered some switching into U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  Around 0640 GMT (2:40 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7506 against the U.S. dollar, compared with HK$7.7484 late Thursday. The Hong Kong dollar has traded between HK$7.7495 and HK$7.7507 so far Friday. \par \par \uc2  Until Mar. 31, HK$7.7500 was seen as a key level triggering Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  defense of the local unit. But as a result of phased devaluation, the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is still comfortably distant from Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level of HK$7.7523. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the weakening in the local unit is predictable, noting that the volatile overnight Hong Kong interbank offered rate is at 4.00%, down from 4.1875% late Thursday, and 75 basis points below its U.S. counterpart. \par \par \uc2  "We are being driven by arbitrage activity," a dealer at an Australian bank said, noting, however, that inflows of cash into the stock market are largely canceling out the effect of the U.S. dollar buying. \par \par \uc2  At 0657 GMT, the blue-chip Hang Seng Index is up 320.09 points, or almost 2.5%, to 13,253.63, on hefty turnover of HK$11.49 billion as overseas funds pile into the stock market. The benchmark index has risen by almost 22% so far this month, and is at its highest level since the Asian crisis first hit the Hong Kong market in Oct. 1997. \par \par \uc2  Forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums are generally higher, in line with the weakening in the spot Hong Kong dollar, but aren't seen rising significantly while the stock market remains firm. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the one-month premium is quoted at six points, down from eight late Thursday. The three-month premium is quoted at 30 points, up from 27 points previously. The six-month premium is quoted at 175 points, up from 165 previously. The one-year premium is quoted at 790 points, up from 770 previously. \par \par \uc2  - By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2832 2336; sean.kennedy@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 23-04-99 \par \par \uc2  0714GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv4n031pf\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (hong kong near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\